hadiths[618]{hadithnumber,text}:
"4242","This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"4243","The same tradition has been narrated by Sayyidna Khawat bin Jubayr (RA) with reference to some other isnads."
"4244","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: Whoever frees a slave and the slave has any wealth, that wealth will remain with the slave. However, if his master makes an exception, the ruling will be different."
"4245","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: When a person frees a slave, his property also remains with him."
"4246","It is narrated about Sayyiduna Umar (RA) that he had given a decision that the mother of the son would not be sold, she would not be bequeathed, she would not be inherited, her master would continue to benefit from her as long as he lived, and when that master died, the son would be free."
"4247","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) forbade the sale of Umm-Wald. He said: They shall not be sold. He will live, he will benefit from them and when he dies, she will be considered independent."
"4248","The same hadith is narrated from Sayyiduna Umar (may God be pleased with him) with reference to another chain of transmission, and it is not narrated as a \marfu'\"" hadith."""
"4249","Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates the statement of Sayyidna Umar (RA) that he forbade the sale of Umm-Wald, “She cannot be given away, “She shall not be divided in inheritance,” Her master will continue to benefit from her during his lifetime, and when the master dies, she will be considered as free."
"4250","Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) forbade the sale of Umm-Wald. They cannot be sold. They cannot be given away."
"4251","Sayyidna Jabar bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: We used to sell our mothers and children as maidservants and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was alive at that time."
"4252","Sayyidna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) says about Umm-Wald that during the time of the Holy Prophet (PBUH), we used to buy and sell her."
"4253","This tradition is narrated along with another document, however, it contains these words: We used to sell the mother of the child during the time of the Holy Prophet (peace be upon him)."
"4254","Saeed bin Musayyib narrates: Sayyidna Umar (RA) declared the mothers and children of female slaves free."
"4255","It is narrated about Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him): Once he had separated a slave girl from her child, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade him from doing so and terminated the transaction."
"4256","Sulaiman bin Yasarbayan narrates: Once I was sitting with Sayyidna Zayd bin Thabit, may Allah be pleased with him. A young man from the Ansar came to him and said: I have a cousin of whom I am a guardian. Peace be upon you. Abu Bakr-e-Nami, the narrator, said: This hadith is: \Gharib\""."""
"4257","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) says: The children of the concubines will be considered free with their freedom and slaves with their slavery."
"4258","Sayyidna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that during the time of the Holy Prophet (may peace be upon him), a man freed his slave. There was 'he had allowed that his services could be sold. The narrator of this tradition is Abdul Ghaffar \weak\"" and other narrators have quoted it as a \""Mursal\"" tradition with reference to the narrator named Abu Ja'far."""
"4259","Narrator Abu Ja'farnami (probably Imam Baqir) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sold the services of a concubine."
"4260","A narrator named Abu Jaafar narrates: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, sold the services of a slave girl. A narrator named Abu Bakr narrates: This is the only hadith I could find about this, and the narrator named Abu Jaafar is reliable, but his tradition is \Mussal\""."""
"4261","Sayyidna Jabar bin Abdullah (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said: There is no harm in selling the services of a counselor while he is in need. This hadith is incorrect as it is transmitted with reference to a narrator named Ibn Tarif. The correct tradition is that it was narrated by a narrator named Abdul Malik as a \Mursal\"" tradition from a narrator named Abu Ja'far and this tradition has already passed."""
"4262","Sayyidna Jabir (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) ordered the sale of mudbar."
"4263","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: The executor (the decision to free the deceased) will be from one-third of the property."
"4264","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: A slave cannot be sold, nor can he be given away. This hadith has only been narrated by a narrator named Ubaidah bin Hasan with a chain of transmission and this narrator is weak."
"4265","It has been narrated about Sayyiduna Abdullah Bin Umar (RA): He considered it abhorrent to sell a Madbar. This tradition is authentic and this tradition is “Muquf”."
"4266","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that once a person died, he left a slave and left some debt. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered his heirs to sell the slave to pay off the debt. So they sold the slave for eight hundred dirhams. Abu Bakranami Muhaddith stated that these words of the hadith: A person died, the narrator made a mistake in this because other narrators have narrated this: (His master himself freed the slave) The Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, while paying the price of this slave to his master, said that you should pay off your debt through him. At that time his master was alive."
"4267","It is narrated about Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) that once she fell ill, one of her nephews mentioned her illness to a person belonging to the Zat tribe who was a doctor, and that person said: The woman you are talking about has been bewitched and this magic was done by one of her maidservants, who had a child in her lap at that time, and the child urinated on the woman's lap. The nieces reported this to Sayyida Ayesha, and Ayesha said, \Bring such and such a slave girl to me.\"" They said about one of their female slaves: \""So these people said that she has a child in her lap.\"" The one who had urinated on Sayya Ayesha's lap. But what was the magic? So he replied: Yes! Sayyida Aisha inquired: Why them? She replied: I wanted you to set me free. So Saida Aisha freed this slave girl as a counselor. Then Saida Aisha said: Now in the name of Allah"," it is necessary for me to say that you will never be free. Who is very rich and sell it to a slave girl. Then Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) bought another slave girl for her price and set her free."""
"4268","It has been narrated about Ibn Sirin, 'He did not think there was anything wrong with a man paying the price of his wife's maidservants himself."
"4269","It is narrated about Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) or perhaps Sayyidna Abdullah Bin Umar (RA) that he says: There is nothing wrong with a pregnant woman or a lactating woman not fasting for a day or a few days in the month of Ramadan."
"4270","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Whoever takes an oath about an oath and thinks that he will fulfill it and then fails to do so, his sin will be on the person who did not allow it to be fulfilled."
"4271","Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: A woman sent her a plate containing dates. Sayyida Ayesha (may Allah be pleased with her) ate some dates from it and left some dates. She said: I swear to you that you will eat all of them. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fulfill it."
"4272","Abu Abd al-Rahman Salmi narrates that once after the sun had set, Sayyiduna Hudhayfah (RA) thought it appropriate that he should fast, so he fasted."
"4273","Abu Abd al-Rahman narrates: After the sun had set, Sayyiduna Hudhayfah (RA) intended to fast and fasted."
"4274","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: If a person looks into his neighborhood (or someone's house) and another person hits his eye with a stone, there will be no retribution for him."
"4275","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: I have been given the most concise words, so I complete the matter in short words."
"4276","It is narrated with the same document that Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said to me: “The Qur’an is very soft, in which there are many aspects, so you should apply it to the situation that is best for you.”"
"4277","Sayyidna Jabar bin Abdullah (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: My words cannot abrogate the words of Allah, but the words of Allah can abrogate my words, and one part of Allah's words can abrogate another."
"4278","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: Like the abrogation of the Qur'an, our hadiths also abrogate each other."
"4279","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Zubair (RA) narrates that I swear by my father, “He told me that sometimes the Prophet (PBUH) used to say something, and then after some time, he would abrogate it."
"4280","Sayyiduna Umar bin Al-Khattab Radiyallahu Anhu says: Avoid those who follow your own opinion, because they will be enemies of the Sunnah, they will not be able to remember the hadiths and will explain the commandment through their own opinion, they will be misguided and mislead others as well."
"4281","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: The children of Israel fell victim to destruction when the children of captive women began to create new things in them."
"4282","Sayyida Umima bint Ruqiqa, may Allah be pleased with her, narrates a similar hadith regarding the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"4283","Sayyida Umeema bint Ruqiqa, the aunt of Sayyida Fatimah, the daughter of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, narrates: We pledged allegiance to the Holy Hand of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"4284","Sayyida Umima bint Ruqiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: We came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to pledge allegiance. We said: O Messenger of Allah! We pledge allegiance to Your Holy Hand that we will not associate anyone with Allah, We will not steal, We will not commit adultery, We will not kill our children, We will not falsely accuse anyone on our behalf, And we will not disobey You in any good deed. The Messenger is more merciful towards us than our own selves, O Messenger of Allah! Extend your holy hand so that we may pledge allegiance to you. The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I do not shake hands with women."
"4285","Bakarbin Abdul Aziz narrates his grandfather's statement regarding his father: Whenever the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) received some good news, he would go into prostration before Allah."
"4286","Sayyiduna Zubair (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) forbade us to fight on behalf of the polytheists, but we will fight on behalf of the responsible people."
"4287","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said that Allah, the Exalted, said: O son of Adam! There are two characteristics in you which were not in you before, one is that when you overcome your anger, I will increase your wealth in order to purify you, and the other is that when your life is complete, my servants will continue to pray for you."
"4288","Sayyidna Mu'awiyah bin Qura'ah narrates on the authority of his father that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: The person whose time of death approaches and he makes a will, according to the order of the Book of Allah, if he has a will, it will become an atonement for what he was not able to pay Zakat."
"4289","Sayyidna Mu'adh bin Jabal (RA) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (PBUH): \Allah has given you one-third of your wealth at the time of your death as a charity"," so that you may increase your good deeds"," so that it becomes a source of purity in your actions.\"""""
"4290","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): No one has the right to have any property in his possession in which he has to make a will, and then two nights pass (that he has not written that will), his will should be written with him."
"4291","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said: No Muslim has the right to have property that he has to make a will and then two nights pass (that he has not made a will), his will should be in writing with him."
"4292","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not proper for a person that three days should pass in such a way that he has such property that he should bequeath (and he did not make a bequest)."
"4293","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (PBUH): It is a great sin to harm someone (an heir) while making a will."
"4294","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: A man should write in his will that if I die without changing my will (so it will be)."
"4295","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said: It is not permissible to make a will for an heir, but if other heirs wish (then the ruling will be different)."
"4296","Sayyidna Amro bin Al-Khajri (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: A will is not for an heir, but if the other heirs want it (it can be)."
"4297","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said: It is not permissible to make a will for an heir, but if the other heirs wish (it can be done)."
"4298","Imam Ja'far Sadiq (may Allah have mercy on him) narrates with reference to his father that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will be no will for the heir, nor will there be acknowledgment of debt (in the property of the inheritance)."
"4299","Sayyidna Amroo bin Al-Khajri (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) while giving a sermon to us in Mina, said this: Allah has determined the share of each one of you in the estate. Therefore, it is not permissible to make a bequest to an heir."
"4300","The same is true of the same (past) Hadith with a different Sunad."
"4301","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was present in the house of Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with him) along with some of his other pure wives, all of whom were waiting for food. The narrator said: This was before the decree of hijab was revealed. Sayyida Aisha grabbed it and broke it. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took it with his hand and mixed it. He sent Sayyida Hafsa (RA) and gave the broken cup to Sayyida Ayesha (RA) as if it had been decided that whoever breaks something will get it and he will be required to pay for it."
"4302","Sayyiduna Abdullah Bin Abbas Radiyallahu Anhuma narrates about the saying of Allah Ta'ala: \And when the Prophet said something in a whisper to one of his wives.\"" He says: Sayyida Hafsa saw the Prophet (may God bless him and grant him peace). He was present at that time with the mother of Sayyidna Ibrahim (may Allah be pleased with him). The Prophet said: You should not tell Aisha about this. Sayyida Hafsa (may God be pleased with her) went to Sayyidah Hafsa (may God be pleased with her) and she told Sayyida Ayesha (may God be pleased with her)"," then Allah informed the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about it. That's why you didn't mention this."""
"4303","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: Earlier people used to write this at the beginning of their wills: This is the will that So-and-so bin So-and-so has made. He testifies that there is no god but Allah. He is one god. He would revive all the people present, then he would exhort his survivors to fear Allah Almighty and work in peace with each other, obey Allah and His Messenger, if they believe, and he is giving them the will that Sayyiduna Ibrahim (peace be upon him) made to his sons: O my sons! Indeed, Allah Ta'ala has chosen a religion for you, so when you die, then become a Muslim."
"4304","Sayyidna Jabar bin Abdullah Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: Once I decided to go to Khyber. I attended the service of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he was in the mosque at that time. I greeted him. Sayyidna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: When you go to my lawyer in Khyber, take fifteen wasqs from him. For the family of Muhammad, there are only those dates in Khyber. If he asks you for a sign (i.e. evidence), you should place your hand on his collarbone. After that, he mentioned the entire hadith. Khabarwahid' makes action necessary."
"4305","Sayyiduna Anas (RA) narrates that Sayyidna Abu Talha, Sayyidna Abi Bin Ka’b and Sayyidna Suhail Bin Bayda (RA) were sitting next to Sayyidna Abu Talha (RA) drinking wine made from dates and chawhars. Anas! Pour out the wine in your vessel.' He said this when we came to know about this, then Sayyiduna Anas (RA) says that I poured out the wine. Shaykh Abu Abdullah i.e. Ubaidullah bin Abdul Samad says: This indicates that the news makes the action necessary."
"4306","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (RA) narrates that when poetry was mentioned before the Prophet (PBUH), he said: It is like speech."
"4307","This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"4308","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amro bin Al-Aas (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (PBUH) said this: Poetry is like speech."
"4309","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A good poem is like a good speech and a good poem is like a good speech."
"4310","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (PBUH): It is not necessary to pay jizya on a Muslim."
"4311","Amro bin Shuaib narrates the statement of his grandfather regarding his father that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Evidence must be presented against the claimant and an oath must be taken against the person against whom the claim is made."
"4312","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: If people start giving according to their claims, then people will start making claims about the lives and property of others."
"4313","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: An oath means that which is confirmed by your companion."
"4314","This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"4315","This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"4316","This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"4317","Sayyidna Udi bin Hatim (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said: Vows are of two types: the one who makes a vow for the sake of Allah, he should fulfill it, and the one who makes a vow related to disobedience to Allah, then his expiation is the same as the expiation for breaking an oath."
"4318","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: Whoever makes a vow and does not mention his name, his expiation will be the expiation of breaking an oath, and whoever takes a vow related to disobedience to Allah, then his expiation will be the expiation of breaking an oath, and whoever makes a vow and that vow is not in his power (i.e., he cannot fulfill it), then his expiation will be the atonement of breaking an oath. There will be expiation, and whoever makes a vow in the name of Allah Ta'ala that he can fulfill, then he should fulfill it."
"4319","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: A vow is only about that thing in which the commandment of Allah has been obeyed."
"4320","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: Whoever makes a vow of disobedience to Allah, the expiation for him will be the same as the expiation for breaking an oath. If he sends a gift to the Kaaba without seeking the pleasure of Allah, then his expiation is the same as the expiation of breaking an oath, and whoever donates his wealth to the poor for a purpose that is not for the sake of Allah, then his expiation is the same as the expiation of breaking an oath, and the person who is obliged to walk to the house of Allah on foot, and it is for such a reason that he If the purpose is not to seek the pleasure of Allah, then his expiation is the same as the expiation of breaking an oath. Whoever makes a vow to walk to the house of Allah on account of something that the purpose is to seek the pleasure of Allah, then he should ride. If he does not go on foot, when he reaches Mecca, he will fulfill his vow. If the desire is achieved, then he should fear Allah and try to fulfill it until he becomes tired of the vow (i.e. he is unable to fulfill it)."
"4321","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said: “Whoever makes a vow that he does not specify, his expiation is that of breaking an oath, and whoever makes a vow that he does not have the power to fulfill, then his expiation is the same as expiation for breaking an oath, and whoever makes a vow that he can fulfill, he should fulfill it."
"4322","Ibn Harmala narrates that a person asked Saeed bin Musaib a question. He said: I have vowed that I will walk to the House of Allah. So he replied: No! Taksaid said: Nothing is obligatory on you."
"4323","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) passed by a man named Abu Israel who was standing in the sun. The Prophet (PBUH) inquired: What is the matter with him? I told him that he made a vow that he would not speak and would not come into the shade and would not sit and would fast. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Tell him to talk, come into the shade, sit down and fast."
"4324","The same is true of the same (past) Hadith with a different Sunad."
"4325","The same hadith has been narrated along with another chain of transmission on the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"4326","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that once the Prophet (PBUH) passed by Abu Israel (after that, the narrator narrated the hadith according to the previous hadith)."
"4327","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that once while the Prophet (PBUH) was giving a sermon, he saw a man who was standing in the sun. The Prophet (PBUH) inquired about him, and the people told him that he was Abu Israel. Let him come even in the shade, let him talk, but he should fast."
"4328","Sayyiduna Abdullah Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: There are four types of oaths, two types of oaths must be expiated and two types of oaths are not expiated. A person who takes this oath: By Allah! We will never do that, and then he has to do it. A person who says: By Allah! I will do that, then he does not do that. As for the two types of oaths in which expiation is not granted, they are if a man swears that I did not do that and although he did that, or a man swears that he did this but he did that (there will be no expiation for him)."
"4329","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) says: Every exception that is incompatible with an oath, then the person who does this will be an oath breaker."
"4330","Sayyidna Amroob bin Shuaib narrates his grandfather's statement regarding his father: Sayyidna Abu Zarghafari (RA) came riding the camel of the Prophet (PBUH) on a camel. If you give me salvation while riding a camel, then I will definitely eat its liver and the flesh of its hump. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: You have given him a great reward."
"4331","Sayyidna Abu Rafi' (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that his freed maid intended to separate Sayyidna Abu Rafi' (may Allah be pleased with him) and his wife. He said one day: If she does this, she will be a Jew. his He asked Sayyida Aisha, Sayyida Abdullah bin Umar, Sayyida Abdullah bin Abbas, Sayyida Hafsa and Sayyida Umm Salma about this, and they all said to him: Do you want to become like Harut and Marut? Then all of them instructed him to make expiation of his oath and leave the pursuit of both of them."
"4332","Narrated Abu Rafi': My freed slave girl said: I will make a separation between you and your wife. If I can do this, all her property will be in the name of the Kaaba and she will be a Jew, a Christian or a Magi on that day. If she cannot separate between you and your wife. Sayyidna Abu Rafi' (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I attended the service of Umm al-Mu'minin, Sayyida Umm Salama (may God be pleased with him), and I said: My freed slave girl wants to create a separation between me and my wife. Sayyida Umm Salama (may God be pleased with her) said: Go to your slave girl and tell her that it is not permissible for you to do this. He said, 'He came' until he came to the door and said: Here are Harut and Marut. This maid said: I have given all my property to the treasure of the Kaaba. He said: I said: I will be a Jew on that day or a Christian or a Magian on that day (if I did not separate between them) then Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar Radiyallahu Anhuma said: If you accept Judaism, you will be killed. He said: Make expiation for your oath and do not cause separation between this person and his wife."
"4333","Qasim narrates: A woman came to Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas, may Allah be pleased with her. She vowed that she would slaughter her son, so Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, ordered her to make expiation, and one of the people present said: Subhan Allah! Atonement will be given for the disobedience of Allah Ta'ala. Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) said: Yes! Allah Ta'ala has made Zahar and ordered expiation for it too (Tazahar is also a disobedience to Allah, but expiation is given for it)."
"4334","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) says: The type of expiation is to give one mudd of wheat to every poor person."
"4335","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) says: Every poor person will be given a helping of wheat along with curry."
"4336","Sayyidna Zaid bin Thabit (RA) says about the type of expiation that one mud of wheat will be given to a poor person."
"4337","Ata narrates: I heard Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah Radiyallahu Anhu saying in a Masjid: One of three things will be given a “mad” in expiation for breaking an oath, in expiation for zahar and in ransom for feeding the poor."
"4338","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) says: Every poor person will be given a \muad\"" of wheat"," along with curry."""
"4339","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) says: When an old person is unable to keep fast, he will feed one meal for one day."
"4340","Amro bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: When a woman claims to divorce her husband and she presents a just witness about it, her husband will be sworn in. If he swears, the testimony of that witness will be invalidated, and if he refuses to swear, then his refusal will be considered as the substitute of the other witness, and his divorce will be recognized."
"4341","Amir al-Shaabi narrates: Two Christian people living in \Daquqa\"" became witnesses to the will of a Muslim. This Muslim had left with the people about whom the will was made. They had doubts about it. We did not get any price in return for it and we did not hide any testimony in the name of Allah Ta'ala. If we do that"," we will be sinful. Sayyiduna Abu Musa Ash'ari (RA) said: This is a decision that has not been made before today after the departure of the Prophet (PBUH)."""
"4342","Adi bin Adi narrates the statement of his father: Two men came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with their case. The case was about a piece of land. One of them said: This is my land and the other said: It is mine. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said about this that the person who has land will take an oath. When he was ready to take the oath, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If that person takes an oath to seize the property of a Muslim, when he appears in the court of Allah, Allah will be angry with him."
"4343","This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"4344","Sayyidna Anas bin Malik (RA) narrates that on the day of the conquest of Makkah, the Prophet (PBUH) granted safety to all but four people. They were Abdul Uzza bin Khatl, Muqis bin Sababah, Abdullah bin Saad and Umm Sarah. As for Abdul Uzza, he was killed. He was hiding in the curtains of the Kaaba."
"4345","Musab bin Saeed narrates this statement of his father: On the day of the conquest of Makkah, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) granted safety to all the people except four men and two women. He said: They (six persons) must be killed, even though you find them hidden in the curtains of the Kaaba: Ikrama bin Abu Jahl, Abdullah bin Khatl, Muqis bin Sababah, Abdullah bin Saad."
"4346","This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"4347","Umar ibn Uthman narrates his grandfather's statement regarding his father that on the day of the conquest of Makkah, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There are four people whom I will not allow anywhere in the \Hal\"" and the \""Haram\""."""
"4348","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may God be pleased with him) narrates: Tamim Dari and Udi bin Bada used to go to Makkah for trade. At the same time, a man belonging to the Banusham tribe was going. He died in a place where no Muslim lived. He came to the service of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked him to take an oath: And he said: \Swear by the name of Allah and say that you have not hidden anything from this and you have no knowledge of it.\"" After that"," the bowl was found in Makkah"," and the person from whom it was found said that I had bought it from Adi bin Bada and Tamim. The heirs obtained that cup and this verse was revealed about them:"""
"4349","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that Tamim Dari and Adi used to come to Makkah. Once a young man from the Banusham tribe was going with them. He died in a place where no Muslim was present. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) swore to them both in the name of Allah that we have not hidden anything and we are not aware of such a thing. Then later that vessel was found in Makkah, so these people said: We bought it from Adi and Tamim. The testimony should be more truthful than the other two (i.e. it is true) and if we do anything wrong, then we will be counted among the wrongdoers. Then these people obtained this vessel. This verse was revealed about these people:"
"4350","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that a Jewish man and a Jewish woman were brought to the service of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Both of them had committed adultery. The Jews said: We used to do this when they were in our possession, but when our possession ended, it is no longer in our power. The Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said to them: Bring to me two of your greatest scholars. They brought to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the two sons of Surya. It is said: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then I ask you both by the name of Allah, who revealed the Torah to Sayyiduna Musa, what punishment have you found for these two (criminals) in the Torah? So they both said: The person who is with a woman will be punished. The person who is seen on a woman's stomach will be punished. But when four men will testify that they saw this person insert his private parts inside the woman, the way the inner stitches of the head are inserted (then they will be stoned). The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: Bring witnesses! Then the four men testified, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stoned them both."
"4351","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) has narrated this: Allah has forgiven my ummah for the sins committed through omission and compulsion."
"4352","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said: May Allah Ta'ala do it or do it deliberately (Tawa will not be punishable)."
"4353","Sayyidna Wasthla bin Asqa' and Sayyidna Abu Umamah (RA) narrate that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: The Yamin is not required on the person who is forced to do so."
"4354","Abu Zubayr states that he asked Sayyiduna Jabir, may God be pleased with him: What do you think that sanctity is proved once through reza'at? He replied: Yes!"
"4355","Mujahideen narrates that Sayyidna Ali and Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with them) say: Rizaat, whether it is small or large, proves sanctity."
"4356","Sayyidna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) (the next hadith), while Sayyida Aisha also narrated this saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) The words of one of them are: \Sucking once or twice does not prove haram\""."""
"4357","Sayyida Aisha has also narrated this statement of the Holy Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him. The words of one of them are: \Sucking once or twice does not prove haram\""."""
"4358","Abu Musa Hilali narrates the statement of his father that once a man was traveling, his wife gave birth to a child, but the woman's milk did not flow, so the man was afraid of the woman, so he began to suck the woman's breast, due to which the milk reached his throat. It has become haram for you. Then he came to Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud, may Allah be pleased with him. He asked him about this, and he told him that the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: It is the feeding that proves haram that produces meat and causes bones to grow (i.e., that which is at a young age)."
"4359","Sayyidna Zayd bin Thabit (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: Drinking Yadu Martaba (one sip) once does not prove Haram."
"4360","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: Sucking once or twice does not prove sanctity. Ibrahim narrates that I mentioned this tradition to Saeed bin Musayb, and he said: When even a drop of milk reaches the stomach of a child while it is still small, then it becomes haraam for it. While the narrator named Uthman has quoted these words that sanctity is proved only by the one who irrigates the bowels with milk, he did not quote any other words."
"4361","The sons of Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud (RA) narrate: Once a man was traveling with his wife. This woman gave birth to a child and the child could not suck milk. The husband of that woman began to suck her milk until he felt the taste of the milk in his throat. The person came to Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud Radi Allahu Anhu, then Sayyidna Abdullah Bin Masud Radi Allahu Anhu came to Sayyidna Abu Musa Ash’ari Radi Allahu Anhu and said: He has given this fatwa, while the Holy Prophet (Sallallahu Alaihi Wasallam) said this: Breastfeeding is what strengthens the bone and produces the flesh."
"4362","Abu Atiyyah narrates: A man came to Sayyidna Abu Musa Ash'ari (RA) and said: My wife had a swelling in her breast. I sucked it and a little milk went down my throat, so Sayyidna Abu Musa Ash'ari (RA) scolded him severely. He replied: Yes! Narrated by Sayyidna Abu Musa (RA) and he scolded me severely about this. So Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud (RA) came to Sayyidna Abu Musa Ash'ari (RA) and said: Is this person a milk drinker? Sayyidna Abu Musa Ash'ari (RA) said: As long as there are such great scholars among you, you people do not ask me any problem: Do it."
"4363","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) says: After two years have passed, adoption is not valid."
"4364","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Only the breastfeeding that takes place within two years is valid."
"4365","Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) says: In the case of a minor, breastfeeding is only done within two years."
"4366","Sayyidah Umm Fazl (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about sucking a sip, does it prove sanctity? So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No! Abu Hamdanami the narrator has quoted these words; A person from Banu Umar said: O Allah?? The prophet! Does sucking once prove haram? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No!"
"4367","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: Sucking once or twice does not prove sanctity; sanctity is proven by one who irrigates the bowels."
"4368","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: A woman came to the service of the Prophet (PBUH) and she said: \So-and-so has married.\"" While I have breast-fed both of them"," the Prophet (PBUH) asked: \""Did you breast-feed them?\"" So the woman replied: I breastfed this girl when she was six and a half years old and I breastfed the child when he was three years old. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Go and tell her to live happily with her wife"," because breastfeeding after the age of breastfeeding does not prove the order of breastfeeding."""
"4369","Sayyiduna Uqbah bin Harith narrates: I married a woman. A black woman came to us and said: I have breastfed you both. (The narrator says:) I attended the service of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. I said: I have married the daughter of so-and-so. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned away from me. I came in front of him from the other side and I said: She is lying. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What can happen now? While he has stated that he has nursed both of you, you separate this woman (i.e. your wife) from you."
"4370","Sayyidna Uqbah bin Harith (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that I had married the daughter of Abu Ahab and a black woman came and said: I have breastfed you both (husband and wife). When asked for the third time, he said: What can happen now? While this has been stated, the narrator says: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stopped this gentleman from establishing a relationship with this woman."
"4371","This tradition is narrated along with another document, which contains these words: I married the daughter of Abu Ahab."
"4372","Sayyidna Uqbah bin Harith (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: A black woman came and she stated that I had breastfed them both (husband and wife). Sayyidna Uqbah's wife was the daughter of Abu Ahab. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned away from her."
"4373","Sayyidna Uqbah bin Harith (RA) narrates that I married a woman, a black woman came to her, she asked me something, but I delayed in giving it to her, so she said: You confirm this to me. By Allah! I have breast-fed both of you husband and wife. The narrator says: I attended the service of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and I mentioned this to him. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: Separate your wife from yourself. There is no good in her for you."
"4374","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: My uncle Aflah bin Abul Qais asked permission to enter my house after the decree of hijab was revealed, so I did not give him permission. I was breastfed by a woman, I was not breastfed by a man. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You should have given him permission because he is your uncle."
"4375","Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (may God be pleased with her) narrates that Abul Qays's brother Aflah came and asked for permission to enter. He was the foster brother of Sayyida Ayesha (may God be pleased with her). This was after the revelation of the Hijab. (to come in) allowed."
"4376","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: First, this verse was revealed in which stoning was ordered, and the verse was revealed in which it was ordered that feeding an older child ten times proves breastfeeding."
"4377","Amro bin Dinar narrates: Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, was asked about any issue of nursing, and he said: According to my knowledge, Allah Almighty has declared the foster sister to be haram. Abdallah bin Zubair was very happy with his decision."
"4378","Amro bin Sharid narrates that Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) was asked about a person who has a wife and a concubine, 'one of them gives birth to a child and the other gives birth to a girl', so would it be permissible for the child to marry the girl of that concubine? So he replied: No! Because sperm is one."
"4379","Sayyida Zainab bint Abu Salama (RA) narrates: Sayyida Asma bint Abu Bakr (RA) breastfed me, so (Syida Asma’s husband) Sayyida Zubair (RA) used to come to me even when I was combing her hair. I have brothers. After that, shortly before the incident of Jarrah, Abdullah bin Zubair (who was my foster brother) asked for my daughter's relationship for his son Hamza, Hamza and Musab, both of whom were the sons of such and such a woman. I am your brother and the children of Sayyida Asmaa (RA) are your brothers. But the children of Sayyidna Zubair who are from children other than Sayyida Asmaa (RA) are not your brothers and sisters. Does not prove."
"4380","Sayyida Umm Fazl (RA) narrates that I heard the Prophet (PBUH) saying that drinking one or two sips does not prove Haram."
"4381","Sayyida Umm Fazl (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was present in my house. I have a wife, and I married another woman after that, so my first wife said, 'She has breastfed my wife', who had breastfed her once, maybe twice, and had given her a yadug lip (the narrator has doubts about this), then the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Filling one yadug lip (the narrator has doubts, perhaps these words are: drinking a yadug twice) does not prove haram."
"4382","Sayyidah Umm Fazl (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said: Drinking a single lip balm does not prove haram. A narrator named Qatadah has quoted these words: By sucking once or twice (it does not prove sanctity)."
"4383","Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Sucking twice does not prove haram."
"4384","Sayyida Aisha (RA) says: In the Qur'an, the command to suck ten specified times was first revealed. Sayyida Aisha (RA) meant that the breast-feeding which proves its sanctity must be sucked ten times. After that, the command of five specified times was revealed."
"4385","Sayyiduna Tamim Dari (RA) narrates: I asked the Prophet (PBUH) about a person who accepts Islam at the hands of another person. The Prophet (PBUH) said: That person will be considered closer to him in life and death than all other people."
"4386","Sayyiduna Abu Umamah Radiyallahu Anhu narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: Whoever accepts Islam on someone else's hand, then that other person will be the owner of the previous one's wealth."
"4387","Sayyiduna Tamim Dari (RA) narrates that I asked the Prophet (PBUH) about a person who accepts Islam at the hands of another person, and he said: He will be closer to him in life and death than all other people."
"4388","Sayyiduna Tamim Dari (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: He asked a person (after that the narrator has mentioned it according to the previous hadith)."
"4389","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about a fallen object, and he said: It is not permissible to use a fallen object. Whoever picks it up will announce it for a year. If its owner comes, he will return it. Will decide about."
"4390","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud Radiyallahu Anhu says: Allah Almighty has completed four things: creation, habit and behavior, sustenance and life."
"4391","Sayyidna Imran bin Hussain (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: A camel named Uzba was owned by a person from Banu Uqeel. This person was taken prisoner. Along with this person, his camel Uzba was also taken prisoner. The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to him. You people have arrested me on the basis of the case and for what reason have you arrested Azba while I am a Muslim? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: If you are saying this, then you are the master of your own affairs (i.e. free) and you will be fully prosperous. Then the man was released in exchange for the ransom of two men. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) put the camel of ``Uzba to ride because she used to travel fast. Once some polytheists robbed a part of Medina at night and captured a Muslim woman. She made a sound. She came to Uzba, but she did not make a sound. It was a camel carrying a great command. That woman rode that camel and came to Madinah. She made a vow that if Allah grants her salvation, she will sacrifice this camel. Peace be upon him is a camel. The narrator narrates: Then this woman was brought to the service of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he was told about her vow, so he said: You have repaid a lot."
"4392","Ata states: The sanctity of breast-feeding is the same as the sanctity of breast-feeding. Once, Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, found out that Abdullah bin Zubair narrates with reference to Sayyida Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, that he said this about breastfeeding: Sucking milk less than seven times does not prove haram, so Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Allah's command, Sayyida Aisha. Better than the saying of the Prophet (may Allah be pleased with him) is what Allah has said: \And your foster sisters.\"" Allah Ta'ala did not say that the reza'at of one time or two times."""
"4393","Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) says: Haram is not proven by breastfeeding less than five times."
"4394","Amro bin Dinar narrates: A person asked Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him: Does it prove sanctity through breastfeeding once or twice? So he said: I understand that a foster sister is forbidden. Then a person said: Amir al-Mu'minin has stated this (this person meant Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Zubair, may Allah be pleased with him) that it is not forbidden by fostering one time."
"4395","This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"4396","Sayyidna Abu Taalba al-Khushai (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: “Allah has prescribed some duties, ‘You shall not waste them’, He has made certain things forbidden, you shall not commit them, and He has set certain limits, ‘You shall not transgress them,’ He has not mentioned anything about certain things without forgetting them, so you should not try to do them.”"
"4397","Sayyidna Amroob bin Harith (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not leave any gold or silver (after Wasal) except a piece of land which he declared as charity and a white mule."
"4398","Sayyidna Amroob bin Harith (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left only his weapons, his white mule and a piece of land in Turkey, which he declared as charity."
"4399","Sayyidna Amroob bin Harith (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) did not leave any dinar or dirham or any slave or any female slave (in Turkey), only his white mule on which he used to ride, his weapons and a piece of land which he gave (as charity) in the name of Allah. A narrator named Qutiba once quoted these words: You called it charity."
"4400","Sayyiduna Amro bin Harith (may Allah be pleased with him) who was the brother of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the brother of his wife Ms."
"4401","Sayyidna Amroob bin Harith (RA) narrates that when the Prophet (PBUH) passed away, he left only his white mule, his weapons and a piece of land in Turkey, which he declared as charity."
"4402","Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the first charity given in Islam was done by Sayyidna Umar (RA). Sayyidna Umar (RA) said: O Messenger of Allah! You advise me what should I do about it? So the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them: Keep this land with you and give its fruits in the way of Allah."
"4403","Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that Sayyidna Umar (RA) said: O Messenger of Allah! I have found a piece of land in Khyber. I have never found a more desirable piece of land. The Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said to him, \If you wish"," give it (the fruit) in charity and keep the original land.\"" Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates: So Sayyiduna Umar (RA) gave it (the fruit) as a charity for his close relatives"," the poor and travelers"," and there is no sin on the person who oversees it"," if he himself is from it. Eats or gives food to one of his friends"," provided that he is a hoarder."""
"4404","Narrated by Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA): Sayyidna Umar (RA) found a land in Khyber called Samagh. He inquired about it from the Prophet (PBUH), and the Prophet (PBUH) said, \Keep this land with you and donate its fruits in charity.\"""""
"4405","Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that Sayyidna Umar bin Khattab (RA) asked the Prophet (PBUH) for permission to donate his land in Shamgh, and the Prophet (PBUH) said: \Give it as a charity in such a way that you distribute its fruits and keep the land with you"," which cannot be sold or inherited.\"""""
"4406","Narrated by Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA): Sayyidna Umar (RA) consulted the Holy Prophet (SAW) about giving his land in Samg in Sadaqah. There are these words in a hadith: You should give it in charity in such a way that its fruits are divided and the original land remains with you so that it cannot be sold or inherited."
"4407","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that Sayyidna Umar (RA) asked the Prophet (SAW) for permission to give the land in Shamgh as charity, and the Prophet (SAW) said: Leave the land with you and give its fruits in the way of Allah."
"4408","Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates the statement of Sayyidna Umar (RA) that I inquired from the Holy Prophet (PBUH) about my land in Shamgh, and the Prophet (PBUH) said, “Leave the land with you and donate its fruits in charity.”"
"4409","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar narrates that he said: O Messenger of Allah! I have made a vow that I will give my property in charity, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Leave the land with you and give its fruits in charity."
"4410","Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that Sayyidna Umar (RA) found a piece of land in Khyber. He came to the Prophet (PBUH) and said, \I have found such a land that no better land has been found before"," so what do you order me about it?\"" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you wish"," let that land remain with you and give its fruits in charity. He properly eats from it 'or gives it to a friend' but the condition is that he is not a hoarder."""
"4411","Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates: Sayyidna Umar (RA) found land in Khyber. He came to the service of the Holy Prophet (SAW). He said: O Messenger of Allah! I have not found any wealth that is better for me, so what do you guide me? So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \If you wish to dedicate the land in the name of Allah"," the original land will remain with you and you give charity from its fruits. Sayyiduna Umar (RA) gave it as charity to the poor"," close relatives"," slaves"," travelers and guests"," and there is no sin on its caretaker if he eats from it properly or feeds it to a friend\"" while he is not a hoarder. The narrators have disagreed about one word of this tradition."""
"4412","This same hadith is narrated along with another document, however, it contains these words: So Sayyiduna Umar gave him charity in such a way that the original land cannot be sold, it cannot be given away, it cannot be divided into inheritance. The narrator then quotes these words at the end: \Let that person be the possessor of wealth.\"""""
"4413","Sayyidna Abdullah Bin Umar (RA) narrates that Sayyidna Umar Bin Khattab (RA) found a piece of land in Khyber. I have found land in Khyber, I have never found a better land than this. What do you order me about it? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you wish, let the earth remain with you and give its fruits in charity. The narrator says: So Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) gave him charity in such a way that the original land could not be sold, given away, or inherited, and its fruit was a charity for the poor, close relatives, slaves, Mujahideen, travelers and guests, and the person who was in charge of it would have no sin if he himself ate from it properly or fed it to one of his friends while he was collecting wealth."
"4414","Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that Sayyidna Umar (RA) narrated that I found a piece of land in Khyber, so I said: O Messenger of Allah! I have found such a land that I have never found the best land. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you want, give it as charity and let the original land remain with you. There would be no sin if he ate some of it himself or fed it to a friend while he was a hoarder. Sayyiduna Umar Radiyallahu Anhu made this will to Sayyida Hafsa Radiyallahu Anhu and then to the older people belonging to the descendants of Sayyidna Umar Radiyallahu Anhu. These words of the hadith are from the narrator Abu Mas'udani, but other narrators have some differences in quoting it."
"4415","This tradition is narrated along with another document, however, it contains these words: the original land cannot be sold, it will not be divided by inheritance."
"4416","The same hadith is also narrated along with another document, however, it contains these words: So they let the original land remain with them in such a way that it should not be sold, not bequeathed, not be inherited, and its fruits should be given as charity to the poor, close relatives, slaves, the needy, travelers and guests."
"4417","Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that Sayyidna Umar (RA) came to the Prophet (PBUH) and said: I have found land in Khyber. In my opinion, I have never found a better land than this. What do you order me about this? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you want to continue, let the land remain with you and give its fruits in charity. There is no sin on him if he properly eats some of it himself or feeds it to a friend while he is a hoarder."
"4418","Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that Sayyidna Umar bin Khattab (R.A.) said that I found land in Khyber. I said: O Messenger of Allah! I have found such a land that I have never found a land that I like more than this and there is no land that is more refined than that. The narrator says: So Sayyiduna Umar gave this land as charity in such a way that it cannot be sold, it cannot be given away, its fruits will be for the poor, close relatives, slaves, guests, travelers, and there will be no sin on the person who takes care of it."
"4419","Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates this statement of Sayyidna Umar Bin Khattab (RA): I found a piece of land in Khyber which was the best for me. I have found land in Khyber, which has been the most abundant for me. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: If you want to keep the land with you and donate its fruits in charity, then Sayyiduna Umar gave it as charity in such a way that it could not be sold, it could not be given away, it would not be inherited. And he who is in charge of it will not be guilty of any sin if he properly eats some of it or properly gives it to a friend while he is a hoarder. Here the narrators have disagreed about one word of the tradition."
"4420","On the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, on the authority of Sayyiduna Umar, a similar narration has been narrated from the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"4421","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that when this verse was revealed: \You people cannot attain goodness until you spend what you like.\"" So Sayyidna Abu Talha (RA) said: O Messenger of Allah! I have a garden in such and such a place. It is a charity for Allah Ta'ala. If I could have given it in secret"," I would not have announced it."""
"4422","The same hadith is narrated along with another chain of transmission, however, these words are added in it: So Sayyidna Abu Talha (RA) named him Sayyidna Abi Bin Ka’b and Sayyidna Hasan Bin Thabit (RA), because these two gentlemen were closer to Sayyidna Abu Talha (RA) than I was."
"4423","This tradition is also narrated along with some other isnads."
"4424","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that when this verse was revealed: \You cannot attain goodness until you spend on what you like.\"" So Sayyidna Abu Talha (RA) said: O Messenger of Allah! Our Lord has asked us for our wealth. I am making you my witness that I dedicate my land in Birha to the name of Allah. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Give it to your close relatives. So Sayyiduna Abu Talha (RA) divided that land between Sayyidna Hasan Bin Thabit and Sayyidna Abi Bin Ka'b (RA)."""
"4425","Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that Sayyidna Umar bin Khattab (RA) said: O Messenger of Allah! According to me, the best wealth is the land whose yield is one hundred wasaqs, which you gave me in Khaybar. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them: Keep the original land with you and give its fruits in charity. The narrator says: So Sayyiduna Umar (RA) wrote this text: This is from 'Umar bin Al-Khattab\ which is about the land of \""Shamgh\"" and about the one hundred wasaqs that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave me which are in Khaybar. I will keep the original of it and give its fruit in charity. \""What will be given to the close relatives"," orphans"," poor travelers and the overseer"," then the overseer himself can eat from it and can also feed one of his friends.\"" But there will be no sin"," but this land cannot be sold"," cannot be given away"," cannot be divided into inheritance"," as long as heaven and earth are established. Sayyiduna Umar (RA) gave this will to his daughter Sayyida Hafsa (RA)"," then if she passed away"," this will would be transferred to another person of opinion from the family of Sayyidna Hafsa (RA)."""
"4426","Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that Sayyidna Umar Bin Khattab (RA) intended to donate his land which was in Shamgh. This was mentioned to the Prophet (PBUH) and he said: \Keep the original land with you and give its fruits in the way of Allah.\"""""
"4427","Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that Sayyidna Umar bin Khattab (RA) said: O Messenger of Allah! I have found a land which is excellent. I want to give it as charity. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You should give it as charity in such a way that the original land cannot be sold, not bequeathed, not shared as an inheritance, and its fruits are spent (in the way of Allah). The narrator says: So Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) gave him charity in the same way, and he wrote in the writing of his charity that it can be given in the way of Allah (i.e. to the Mujahideen) to guests, to travelers, to the poor and to the close relatives of the person who will be the caretaker of this land."
"4428","Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that Sayyidna Umar bin Khattab (RA) said to the Prophet (SAW): I received a hundred shares in Khyber."
"4429","Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that Sayyidna Umar (RA) came to the service of the Holy Prophet (SAW) He became the owner of a hundred shares in Khyber, he also acquired some more land by purchase, then he came to the service of the Prophet (SAW) and said: I have found such a land that has never been found before. So the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Keep the original and give its fruits in the way of Allah."
"4430","Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that Sayyidna Umar (RA) said in the service of the Holy Prophet (SAW) 'After that, it is according to the previous hadith."
"4431","Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that Sayyidna Umar (RA) attended the service of the Holy Prophet (SAW) and he said: O Messenger of Allah! I have found such a land that I have never found such a land. (The narrator says:) Sayyiduna Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, received one hundred shares. He says: I bought one hundred shares from its owners in Khyber through it (i.e. I bought this much land). I want to get close to Allah through it."
"4432","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the statement of Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) that I asked the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the land in Shamgh."
"4433","Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that Sayyidna Umar (RA) said: O Messenger of Allah! I have got land in Shamgh. I dislike that it should be sold after me. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Keep it and give its fruits in the way of Allah."
"4434","Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that Sayyidna Umar bin Khattab (RA) found land in Khyber. He came to the service of the Holy Prophet (SAW). He said: I have found land in Khaybar. I have never found any land that is better than this land. The narrator narrates: So Sayyiduna Umar kept the original land and gave its produce as charity, in such a way that this land cannot be sold, it cannot be given away, it cannot be inherited, its produce will be distributed among the poor, close relatives, guests, Mujahideen and travelers. be"
"4435","Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that Sayyidna Umar (RA) came to the service of the Holy Prophet (SAW) and received one hundred plots of land in Khyber. He bought land and gathered them together. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Leave the original land with you and give its fruits in the way of Allah."
"4436","The judge al-Ḥusayn ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us, Yūsuf ibn Mūsā narrated to us, Jarīr narrated to us, Ḥuṣayn ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān narrated, from ʿAmr ibn Jāwān. And Muḥammad ibn Manṣūr ibn Abī al-Jahm narrated to us, al-Sarī ibn ʿĀṣim narrated to us, ʿAbdullāh ibn Idrīs narrated to us. And it was read to Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Abī al-Shawārib, in my presence, and I heard it being said to him: \Did you hear ʿAbbās ibn Yazīd?\"" He said: \""I heard ʿAbdullāh ibn Idrīs say: 'I heard Ḥuṣayn ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān narrate from ʿAmr ibn Jāwān.'\"" And Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Saʿdān narrated to us"," Shuʿayb ibn Ayyūb narrated to us"," Yaḥyā ibn Ādam narrated to us"," ʿAbdullāh ibn Idrīs narrated"," from Ḥuṣayn ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān"," from ʿAmr ibn Jāwān al-Saʿdī. And ʿAlī ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Mubashshir narrated to me"," Aḥmad ibn Sinān narrated to us"," ʿAlī ibn ʿĀṣim narrated"," from Ḥuṣayn"," who narrated to me: ʿAmr ibn Jāwān al-Māzinī said: \""I heard al-Aḥnaf ibn Qays.\"" And Abū Ṣāliḥ al-Aṣbahānī ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Saʿīd narrated to us"," Abū Masʿūd narrated to us"," Abū Dāwūd narrated to us"," Abū ʿAwwānah narrated"," Ḥuṣayn informed me"," from ʿAmr ibn Jāwān. And Abū Sahl ibn Ziyād narrated to us"," ʿAbdullāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal narrated to us"," my father narrated to us"," Bahz ibn Asad narrated to us"," Abū ʿAwwānah narrated to us"," Ḥuṣayn narrated"," from ʿAmr ibn Jāwān. And Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Zakariyyā narrated to us"," Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Nasāʾī narrated to us"," Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm narrated"," from al-Muʿtamir ibn Sulaymān"," who said: \""I heard my father narrate from Ḥuṣayn ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān"," from ʿAmr ibn Jāwān"," a man from Banī Tamīm. That was because I said to him: 'What do you think about the withdrawal (iʿtizāl) of al-Aḥnaf—what was it?' He said: 'I heard al-Aḥnaf say—while I was performing Ḥajj—we were at our encampment unloading our saddles when a messenger came to us and said: \""The people have gathered in the mosque.\"" I went and found the people assembling"," and among them were a group of men seated. There was ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib"," al-Zubayr"," Ṭalḥah"," and Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ. When I stood over them"," it was announced: \""ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān has come to al-Madīnah.\"" He came wearing a yellow cloak. I said to my companion: \""Stay as you are until I see what he has brought.\"" ʿUthmān said: \""Is ʿAlī here? Is al-Zubayr here? Is Ṭalḥah here? Is Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ here?\"" They said: \""Yes.\"" He said: \""I adjure you by Allah"," besides whom there is no deity—do you know that the Messenger of Allah"," peace and blessings be upon him"," said: 'Whoever purchases the mirbad of Banī So-and-so"," Allah will forgive him'? So I purchased it"," and I came to the Messenger of Allah"," peace and blessings be upon him"," and said: 'I have purchased the mirbad of Banī So-and-so.' He said: 'Make it part of our mosque"," and its reward is for you.'\"" They said: \""Yes.\"" He said: \""I adjure you by Allah"," besides whom there is no deity—do you know that the Messenger of Allah"," peace and blessings be upon him"," said: 'Whoever purchases the well of Rūmah"," Allah will forgive him'? So I came to the Messenger of Allah"," peace and blessings be upon him"," and said: 'I have purchased the well of Rūmah.' He said: 'Make it a watering place for the Muslims"," and its reward is for you.'\"" They said: \""Yes.\"" He said: \""I adjure you by Allah"," besides whom there is no deity—do you know that the Messenger of Allah"," peace and blessings be upon him"," said: 'Whoever equips the Army of Hardship (jaysh al-ʿUsrah)"," Allah will forgive him'? So I equipped them to the point that they lacked neither a hobble nor a bridle.'\"" They said: \""Yes.\"" He said: 'O Allah"," bear witness! O Allah"," bear witness! O Allah"," bear witness!'\"" This is the wording of the ḥadīth of al-Muʿtamir"," from his father"," from Ḥuṣayn. Ibn Idrīs said in his narration: \""Whoever purchases the mirbad of Banī So-and-so"," Allah will forgive him","\"" so I purchased it for twenty thousand or twenty-five thousand. He also said regarding the well of Rūmah: \""I purchased it for such-and-such","\"" then I came to him. He said: \""Make it a watering place for the Muslims"," and its reward is for you.\"" ʿAlī ibn ʿĀṣim said in his narration regarding the story of the mirbad: \""I purchased it for such-and-such"," then I came to the Prophet"," peace and blessings be upon him"," and said: 'I have purchased the mirbad of Banī So-and-so to expand the mosque of the Muslims.' He said: 'Yes"," and its reward is incumbent upon you.'\"" He said regarding the well of Rūmah: \""I purchased it for twenty thousand or twenty-five thousand\""—the doubt being from Ḥuṣayn. Abū Dāwūd said"," from Abū ʿAwwānah"," regarding the story of the mirbad: \""I purchased it for twenty-odd thousand or thereabouts.\"" The remainder of their wordings are close in meaning"," and the import is the same. In the ḥadīth of Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal regarding the well of Rūmah: \""I purchased it for such-and-such.\"""""
"4437","Samama bin Hazan Qashiri narrated that I was at the house of Sayyidna Uthman RA at that time, when Sayyidna Uthman RA looked at the people and said: I ask you people by swearing in the name of Allah, do you know that when the Prophet SAW came to Madinah, at that time there was only a well of fresh water, then the Prophet SAW said: Who By purchasing Bayrumah, he will devote it to the Muslims. In return, he will get Paradise. So I bought it from my property and gave all Muslims equal rights to it, and today you people are preventing me from drinking water from that well, and I have to drink sea water. These people replied: Allah knows that it is so. I am asking if you people know that I provided equipment for the Tabuk campaign from my personal wealth. The people replied: Allah knows that it is so. Then Sayyiduna Uthman Ghani said: I ask you by Allah and Islam that you know that the mosque had become small. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who will buy the land of such and such people for the expansion of the mosque? \He will get Paradise in return"," so I bought him out of my wealth and made an addition to the mosque through him.\"" Today"," you people are preventing me from praying two rak'ahs in the same mosque. They said: \""Allah knows that it is so.\"" Sayyidna Uthman Ghani (RA) said: I ask you people by the name of Allah Almighty and Islam"," do you know that the Prophet (PBUH) was on Mount Sabir in Makkah"," along with him were Sayyidna Abu Bakr"," Sayyidna Umar and I too. There is a Prophet"," a Siddique and two martyrs. The people said: Allah knows that it is like this. Then Sayyiduna Uthman"," may Allah be pleased with him"," said Allahu Akbar"," Allahu Akbar"," and said: You people"," be witnesses about me! By the Lord Kaaba! I am a martyr"," he said this three times. Here the words of tradition are similar to each other."""
"4438","This same hadith has been narrated along with another chain of transmission, however, these words are added in it: I ask you people by the name of Allah, do you know that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married his second daughter to me after the death of one of his daughters? He was pleased with me and was happy with me."
"4439","Tamma bin Hazun Qashiri narrates that I was at the house of Sayyidna Uthman (RA) when Sayyidna Uthman (RA) was martyred. Sayyidna 'Uthman (RA) peeked through the wall of this house and said: Bring your two companions before me, who are the root of the mischief. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Medina, the mosque was too crowded for worshipers, so he said: Who will dedicate this land from his wealth to the Muslims? He will find a better place in Paradise than this. So I bought it from my wealth and dedicated it to the Muslims. The people said: Allah knows that it is so. Then Sayyidna Uthman Ghani said: Now you people are preventing me from offering two rakat prayers from this mosque. I ask you people by swearing in the name of Allah. That's how it is."
"4440","This tradition is narrated along with another chain of transmission, but it contains these words: Where are the two people who incited you against me? Sayyiduna Uthman Ghani (RA) said: I ask you people by the name of Allah, do you know that when the Prophet (PBUH) came to Madinah, there was no sweet well there, there was only Birrumah? So he will be more beautiful than him in heaven, so I bought him from my wealth and today you people are preventing me from drinking water from that well."
"4441","A narrator named Musa bin Hakim narrates that Ibn Amir wrote a letter to Sayyiduna Uthman Ghani, may Allah be pleased with him, and by that time these people had surrounded him. They kept looking and I extended the letter towards them. They read it and then they turned towards the mosque and saw Sayyiduna Talha (RA) sitting in the eastern direction of the mosque. They called out: O Talha! Sayyiduna Talha replied: I am present! Sayyidna Uthman Ghani said: I swear to you in the name of Allah, do you know that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: Who will buy this piece of land and expand the mosque through it? He said: You people are in a state of peace in this mosque and I am in a state of fear. Then Syedna Uthman Ghani said: O Talha! He said: I am present! Then Sayyidna Uthman (RA) said: I swear to you in the name of Allah, do you know that the Holy Prophet (PBUH) said this: Who will buy the well of Rumah and dedicate it to the Muslims? He will get this something in exchange for it. So I bought it from my wealth. He said: 'Allah knows that it is so.' Talha! He said: I am present! So Sayyidna Uthman Ghani (RA) said: I ask you by the name of Allah, do you know that I provided one hundred camels for the Tabuk campaign? Sayyidna Talha (RA) replied: Allah knows that it is so. After that, Sayyidna Talha (RA) said: O Allah! According to my knowledge, Syedna Uthman (RA) is oppressed."
"4442","Sayyidna Abu Salama bin Abdul Rahman narrates that when Sayyidna Uthman Ghani (RA) was surrounded in his house, he looked at the people and swore to them. He said: Do you people know that I was with the Prophet (PBUH) on Mount Hara? The narrator says that the people confirmed this to him. Then Sayyidna Uthman Ghani (RA) said: Do you people know that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: Who will add a house to the mosque? So I bought a house and expanded the mosque through it, so the people confirmed his statement. Do you know that the water of Ruma well was sold only to travelers? I bought this well and dedicated it in the name of Allah. People replied: Yes! The people confirmed this to him. Then Sayyidna Uthman Ghani said: I ask you people by swearing in the name of Allah! Do you people know that I had provided equipment for the battle of Tabuk and I had spent so much money on it, so the people also confirmed this? Then Sayyidna Uthman Ghani, may Allah be pleased with him, said: I have lived among you for so long, but you have shown haste about me that I should take off the khilaat that Allah has made me wear, by Allah! It will never happen."
"4443","Abu Salamah bin Abdul Rahman narrates that Sayyiduna Uthman looked out from his house and saw that it was besieged at that time and said: By the name of Allah, I ask you people, who was there at that time? When the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on Mount Hara and the mountain began to move, the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) struck it with his foot and said: O Hara! Be still. Above you is a Prophet, a Siddique and a martyr. I was also with the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at that time, so some people testified to this (that this is true). Then Sayyiduna Uthman Ghani, may God be pleased with him, said: The person who was with the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, at that time when he took the pledge of allegiance, I ask him in the name of Allah that when the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent me to the polytheists. So he said that this is my hand and this is Uthman's hand. Then the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took the oath of allegiance on my behalf. Some people also confirmed this to him. Then Sayyiduna Uthman Ghani (RA) said: I ask this person through Allah, who was present at the time when the Holy Prophet (PBUH) said this: Who will buy this house and add it to the mosque? So I bought this house from my wealth and expanded this mosque through it. Some people confirmed this to him. Then Sayyiduna Uthman Ghani said: I ask this person in the name of Allah who was with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, at that time when he was preparing for the Tabuk campaign. So I provided half of the army with equipment from my own wealth.' Then Sayyiduna Uthman Ghani, may God be pleased with him, said: I ask this person in the name of Allah, who was present when the water of Rumah was sold only to travelers, so I bought it from my property and dedicated it to travelers (and to all Muslims). Some people also confirmed this."
"4444","This tradition is also narrated along with some other isnads."
"4445","This tradition is also narrated along with some other isnads. However, it contains these words: When Sayyiduna Uthman Ghani was surrounded in his house, some people gathered around his house. Sayyidna Uthman looked at him."
"4446","Abu Abdul Rahman Salmi narrates that when Sayyiduna Uthman Ghani (RA) was besieged, he looked at the people from the roof of his house and said: I am reminding you people of Allah. Do you not know that when the Hara began to move, the Prophet (PBUH) said: O Hara! Stay in your place! There is a Prophet, a Siddiq and a Martyr above you. People replied: Yes! So Sayyidna Uthman Ghani (RA) said: I am reminding you of Allah. Do you know that when the Prophet (PBUH) started providing supplies for the Tabuk campaign, he said: Who will spend such a thing that will be accepted? So the people were in need at that time. I ask if you people do not know that the water from the Ruma well could be drunk only for a price, so I dedicated it to every wealthy, poor and traveler by purchasing it, so these people replied: Yes! After that Sayyidna Uthman Ghani (RA) counted some other things as well."
"4447","Abu Abd al-Rahman Salmi narrates that when Sayyiduna Uthman Ghani (RA) was besieged, he looked at the people and said: I am asking you in the name of Allah, and I am only asking the companions of the Prophet (PBUH) that do you not know that the Prophet (PBUH) said: Whoever digs a well in Rumah (i.e. dedicates it) ga) He will get Jannah, so I dug it. Do you not know that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever provides supplies for the battle of Tabuk, he will receive Paradise. will"
"4448","Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud Radiyallahu Anhu says: Allah Almighty has finished with four things: the creation of man, his morals, his sustenance and his death. It is no longer possible for a person to acquire anything."
"4449","Basheer bin Muhammad narrates about Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Zayd, may Allah be pleased with him, that he gave his garden as charity. That is what we used to live on. We have no wealth other than this. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called Sayyiduna Abdullah and said: Allah has accepted your charity and returned it to your parents."
"4450","Basheer bin Muhammad narrates that his grandfather Sayyiduna Abdullah (RA) gave his wealth in charity. He had no wealth other than this, so the Prophet (PBUH) said to Sayyidna Abdullah (RA): Allah has accepted your charity from you. In quoting the words here, the narrator has quoted some different words (and the Holy Prophet (peace be upon him) said:) and returned it to your parents."
"4451","This tradition is narrated along with another chain of transmission, however, it contains these words: Sayyidna Abdullah bin Zayd (RA) gave his wealth in charity and the parents of Tawan attended the service of the Prophet (PBUH) after that, the narrator has mentioned it according to the previous hadith."
"4452","Sayyidna Abdullah bin Zayd, may Allah be pleased with him, came to the service of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: O Messenger of Allah! This garden of mine is a charity. It is in the name of Allah and His Messenger. So his parents came to the service of the Holy Prophet. They said: O Messenger of Allah! We passed away in this garden, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned that garden to both of them. This hadith is \transmitted\"". The reason for this is that Sayyidna Abdullah bin Zayd (RA) died during the reign of Sayyidna Uthman Ghani (RA)."""
"4453","This tradition is narrated along with another chain of transmission, but it contains these words: This is Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Zayd, may God be pleased with him, who was shown the way to call the call to prayer in a dream, and then he attended the service of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"4454","Amro bin Salim narrates that Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Zayd, who was taught how to call the call to prayer in a dream, gave a garden of his in charity. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned that garden to his parents, then when these parents died, the heirs of Tawan got it."
"4455","Amro bin Salim narrates that Sayyidna Abdullah bin Zaid (RA) gave his garden as charity. He came to the service of the Prophet (PBUH). He said: I dedicate this garden of mine to the Prophet (PBUH)."
"4456","Sayyidna Ubada bin Samit (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that a man named Abdullah bin So-and-so (the narrator named Shaaban has been forgotten here) came to the service of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah! My everything is in charity except my horse and my weapons. The narrator narrates: He also had some land. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took possession of it and assigned it as afaz (i.e. as a financial aid to various people). We don't have anything other than this. We people go round and round about things. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took this garden and handed it over to them both. What I gave in charity and what you returned to my parents, then both of them passed away: O Messenger of Allah! What I gave in charity and what you gave back to my parents, now that they have both passed away, is this halal for me? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Yes! You eat with pleasure."
"4457","Sayyidna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that two men came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with their case, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Sayyidna Amr bin Al-Aas (may God be pleased with him): You decide between them. He said: O Messenger of Allah! In your presence? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Yes! He said: How should I decide? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you do ijtihad and make a correct decision, you will get ten rewards, and if you make a mistake after doing ijtihad, you will get one reward."
"4458","This is narrated along with the hadith and the chain of transmission, but in it the word \goodness\"" has been used instead of reward."""
"4459","Sayyiduna Uqbah bin Aamir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that two men came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with their case, and the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: O Uqbah! Get up and decide between them. I said: O Messenger of Allah! You are more entitled to it. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you used ijtihad while deciding between them and made a correct decision, you will get ten rewards, and if you made a mistake while making ijtihad, you will get one reward."
"4460","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (SAW) that when a person performs ijtihad while making a decision and makes a correct decision, he receives ten rewards, and when a person performs ijtihad while making a decision and makes a mistake, he receives rewards."
"4461","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said: \Whoever wants to be a judge is slaughtered without a knife.\"""""
"4462","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: The person who is made a Qazi is as if he had been slaughtered without a knife."
"4463","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The person who was made a judge was slaughtered without a knife."
"4464","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: When a person who makes a decision performs ijtihad while making a decision and makes a correct decision, he gets rewards, and when he makes a wrong decision while making ijtihad, he gets a reward. \When a Qazi performs ijtihad while making a decision and makes a correct decision"," he gets rewards and when he makes a mistake while making a decision"," he gets a reward.\"""""
"4465","Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): “Whoever is a ruler who makes decisions between people, when he is resurrected on the Day of Resurrection, an angel will take him with a mace and take him to the edge of Hellfire and make him stumble. The distance will be forty years. A narrator named Masrooq narrates: If I make righteous decisions for one day, that is more preferable to me than fighting for a hundred years in the cause of Allah."
"4466","Sayyidah Umm Salma (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: Whoever is tempted to judge between people, he should act justly between people in his behavior, in his gestures, in the way he sits (act justly in all respects)."
"4467","Sayyidah Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: He who is tempted to decide between people should not raise his voice in front of any of the two sides of the case, until he raises his voice in front of the other side as well (i.e. treat both equally)."
"4468","Sayyidah Umm Salamah (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said: \Whoever is tempted to decide between Muslims"," should not decide between two parties in anger.\"""""
"4469","It is narrated about Sayyiduna Abu Bakra that he wrote in a letter to his son who was a judge in Sajistan: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: No judge should judge between two men in a state of anger and should not give two judgments in one case."
"4470","Sayyidna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: A person who makes a decision should make a decision when he is full and has eaten (that is, he should not make a decision in a state of restlessness and indecisiveness or mental disorder)."
"4471","Abul Malih al-Hazli narrates: Sayyidna Umar bin Al-Khattab (RA) wrote a letter to Sayyidna Musa Ash'ari (RA) in which it was written: (Amaafad!) Qada is a duty that is very important and a method that should be maintained. When the evidence comes before you, if the right is clear, then you enforce it, and it is of no use to speak about a right that cannot be enforced. You sit on an equal level with people. It will be obligatory on him who denies it. It is permissible to make peace between Muslims, except for such a peace that makes the forbidden thing lawful and the lawful thing declared forbidden. It is ``to act with understanding'' to act with understanding' about the thing that you are confused about in your mind' and no ruling from the Book or the Sunnah has reached you about it', so in such a case, put other cases like it in front of you and hypothesize the rulings and give preference to that which is more pleasing to Allah Almighty and is more similar to the truth, according to your opinion. The person who has claimed, if he asks for time to present the evidence, give him time to present the evidence, and if the evidence is presented, give a decision according to his right, if not, then give a decision against that person. This is because this situation has become clear even for a blind person and is more eloquent in terms of excuses. Every Muslim is just. They are related to each other. It is that he bears false witness, or whoever is thought to be (giving false witness) because of his lineage because of his guardianship, then take care of him. This is because Allah is the guardian of the inner things, but the punishment will be removed from you on the basis of evidence. Allah will make the reward obligatory. This thing will become a treasure for you in the hereafter. This is because the person whose intention is right in the matter between Allah and the servant, even if that thing is against the person himself, Allah will protect that person from harm in relation to the people, and whoever is adorned with regard to the people, but Allah's knowledge about it will be different, then Allah will disgrace that person. So you want to get wages from someone else instead of Allah Ta'ala? While Allah Ta'ala also gives immediate sustenance and also gives the treasures of His mercy and peace be upon you."
"4472","It is narrated about Saeed bin Abu Barda that once he took out a letter of Sayyiduna Umar (RA) and said: This is the letter of Sayyidna Umar (RA) then a narrator named Sufyan read this letter in front of me in which it was written: But later! Justice is a duty that is necessary and a method that should be maintained. You should understand that when a case comes before you, it does not help you to talk about the right. It is necessary to present evidence and the person who refuses will take an oath. It is permissible to make peace between Muslims, except for a peace that makes a forbidden thing lawful or a lawful thing forbidden. Nothing can invalidate and return to the truth. It is better than a person to continue on falsehood which causes confusion in your mind. To try to understand it in relation to that which has not reached you in terms of the Qur'an and the Sunnah. I came, you give time to the person claiming to present his evidence during this time, if he did, then it is fine, otherwise, to decide against him, because now this situation will become more common for the blind person and will be more eloquent regarding the excuse. All Muslims are just. They are related to each other. Allah Ta’ala is the guardian of the inner things, but based on evidence, you will be removed from Samzak and yes, avoiding disturbing people, persecuting them, and avoiding opposition about the truth from such a place. As a result, Allah Ta’ala will make the reward obligatory. This thing will become a treasure for you in the Hereafter. This is because between Allah Ta’ala and a servant whose intention is right, even if that thing is against him, Allah Ta’ala. He will protect him from harm in relation to people, and whoever has good knowledge about people, but his knowledge about Allah will be different. Allah will disgrace that person. So you should get rewards from someone else instead of Allah. This does not happen in the presence of Allah, Allah disgraces this person."
"4473","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that there will come to you traditions that are different from each other, so whoever comes to him with traditions that are in agreement with the Book of Allah, they will be from me."
"4474","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): If you are told a hadith about me that you understand, and you do not deny it, then you remain silent and confirm it."
"4475","The same hadith is narrated along with another chain of transmission, but it has these words added: The reason for this is that I will say that which is known and which is not \denied\"" and I will not say that which is \""denied\"" and is not known."""
"4476","Sayyiduna Ali bin Abu Talib (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said: After me, there will be some people who will narrate traditions about me, so you should present those traditions on the Qur'an and accept those that are in accordance with the Qur'an, and do not accept those that are not in accordance with the Qur'an. (Imam Dar al-Qati says:) The tradition is illusory. The correct one is that it is narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as a “Mursal” tradition with reference to Asim, with reference to Imam Zayd, with reference to Imam Zain al-Abidin, may God have mercy on him."
"4477","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that two men came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a case regarding a camel, and one of them said: This camel has given birth to a child with me."
"4478","Abu Qais, who is the slave of Sayyiduna Amro bin Al-Aas, narrates: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, has decreed that when a judge performs ijtihaad while giving a decision and makes a mistake about it, he will receive a reward."
"4479","Another hadith is narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Sayyidina Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"4480","Sayyiduna Amro bin Al-Aas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: When a judge performs ijtihad while giving a decision and gives a wrong decision, he will be rewarded for it, and if he gives a correct decision while giving a decision, he will be punished."
"4481",""
"4482","Al-Qamah Bin Wail narrates this on the authority of his father: A man from Hadramout and a man from Qandah came to the service of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Hadrami said: O Messenger of God! This person has taken possession of my land. That land belonged to my father. This person said: That land is mine and I have it. I cultivate it. This person has no right in this land. So he said no! The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) inquired: Then this other party will take an oath. This Hazrami inquired: O Messenger of Allah! It wouldn't care what oath it was taking? Because he does not avoid committing sins. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This is the situation for you. Then this person took an oath. When he left, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If he has taken an oath on another person's property for the purpose of consuming it as an act of injustice, then when he appears in the court of Allah, Allah will turn away from him."
"4483","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that two men claimed ownership of an animal, neither of them had any evidence, so the Prophet (PBUH) ordered them both to take an oath and take part in it."
"4484","The same hadith is narrated along with another chain of transmission, however, it has these words added: \They both agree or do it in a state of compulsion.\"""""
"4485","Imam Jafar Sadiq (RA) narrates this statement of Sayyiduna Jabir (RA): The Prophet (PBUH) gave a decision in favor of a person through a witness and taking an oath."
"4486","Imam Jafar bin Sadiq (RA) narrates on the authority of his father (Imam Muhammad Baqir, may God have mercy on him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took an oath from a person who sought the truth and had a witness with him."
"4487","Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave a decision through the testimony of a person and the swearing of a rightful person. The narrator says that Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) also gave such a decision in Iraq."
"4488","Amro bin Shuaib narrates the statement of his grandfather Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amro, may Allah be pleased with him, regarding his father, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, has said this: Regarding the truth, Allah and His Messenger have ruled in favor of two witnesses: \Whoever brings two witnesses will receive his right.\"""""
"4489","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) gave a verdict by taking an oath with a witness."
"4490","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (SAW) returned the oath of a person who sought the truth."
"4491","Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says: The person against whom a claim has been made will be more entitled to take an oath, but if that person refuses to take an oath, then the person making the claim will take an oath and receive this right."
"4492","Sayyidna Hasan Basri narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: A person who is called to the court of a Muslim (judge) and does not go there, then that person will be a tyrant, he will have no right."
"4493","Rabi'ah bin Abd al-Rahman narrates this regarding the son of Sayyidna Sa'd bin Ubada: We have found this in the writings of Sa'd bin Ubada: \The Holy Prophet"," may God's prayers and peace be upon him"," gave a decision by taking an oath with a witness.\"""""
"4494","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) gave a verdict by taking an oath with a witness. Some narrators have disagreed in narrating it."
"4495","Sayyidna Ali bin Abu Talib (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH), Sayyidna Abu Bakr (Sayyidna Umar), Sayyidna Uthman (RA) used to take an oath from the claimant and give judgments."
"4496","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Aamir (RA) narrates that I agreed to see Sayyidna Abu Bakr (RA), Sayyidna Umar (RA) and Sayyidna Uthman (RA)."
"4497","Adi al-Kindi narrates that two men came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a case. One of them said: This land is mine. It is my property."
"4498","Amro bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, narrates from his grandfather that the Prophet, may God's prayers and peace be upon him, said: He who takes up the profession of wisdom and does not know about it, if any person is harmed as a result of his treatment, he will pay a ransom."
"4499","Amro bin Shuaib narrates the statement of his grandfather on the authority of his father: The person who adopts wisdom even though he is not known for wisdom, and as a result of it someone dies or suffers less damage, then that person will pay the ransom."
"4500","Amro bin Shoaib narrates his grandfather's statement regarding his father that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that a person who becomes a doctor and is not well-known in this profession will pay a ransom."
"4501","Amro bin Shu'ayb narrates his grandfather's statement regarding his father: The claimant has the greater right to present evidence."
"4502","This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"4503","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the wife of a man who had given birth to that man's two children, that woman used to hurt the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He put the crucible until the hoe crossed her body (and the woman died), then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You people, be witnesses! This woman's blood has been wasted."
"4504","This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"4505","This is what was narrated on the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, however, it contains these words: This person said: The other day this woman started cursing you and insulted you, so I killed her. Imam Dar al-Qati has stated that this proves this Sunnah: \When giving a decision"," the ruler can make the people witness about himself.\"""""
"4506","Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that all cities are the cities of Allah, all the servants are the servants of Allah, whoever settles a barren land will get it, and no one can occupy it as an injustice."
"4507","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that it is obligatory for the person who claims to present evidence and for the one who denies it to swear an oath."
"4508","Amro bin Shuaib narrates his grandfather's statement regarding his father that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that it is necessary for a person who makes a claim to present evidence and for a person who denies it, it is necessary to swear an oath."
"4509","Amro bin Shuaib narrates his grandfather's statement regarding his father that the Prophet, may God's prayers and peace be upon him, said: Evidence must be presented against the claimant, and an oath must be taken against the person against whom the claim is made."
"4510","Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the statement of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that the person who makes a claim must be presented with evidence and the person against whom the claim is made must only swear an oath."
"4511","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) has said that the person against whom a claim has been made will have the right to only take an oath, but if evidence is presented (then the ruling will be different)."
"4512","Sayyidna Imran bin Hussain (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered the claimant to produce a double witness and instructed the person against whom the claim was made to take an oath."
"4513","Sayyiduna Zayd Radiyallahu Anhu narrates that a person who receives something from his brother without proof, then the person against whom there is a case, must take an oath."
"4514","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The testimony of a villager will not be valid against a person living in a city."
"4515","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that the testimony of a villager against a citizen will not be accepted."
"4516","Muhammad bin Abu Bakr narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, with reference to his father, Sayyiduna Abu Bakr As-Sadiq (may Allah be pleased with him), saying: The inheritance is divided which can be divided."
"4517","Abd al-Rahman bin Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates on the authority of his father in the same way, in which it is narrated that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This is the inheritance that can be divided."
"4518","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: An Ansari was found dead near the well of the Jews in Khyber. They mentioned this to the Prophet (PBUH). The Prophet (PBUH) sent a message to these people to take 50 people, each of whom swore by name that I did not kill him, nor do I know anything about the murderer. He said: He has given the same ruling as was in the Shari'ah of Sayyiduna Musa (peace be upon him)."
"4519","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A space of up to 25 cubits is protected around a well in the forest, and a space of up to 50 cubits around a well in a village is protected, a space of up to three hundred cubits is protected around a spring flowing in an open place, while a space of six hundred cubits is protected around a spring flowing near a farm."
"4520","Sayyidna Abaid bin Hamal narrates that he requested the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to give him a piece of land called \Malh Shaza\"" at the location of \""Ma'rib\""; the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave that place to him. I had reached this place in the time of Jahiliyyah. It was a place where the water had no name and no sign. The person who reached there used to occupy it. The example of this was flowing water. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took back that place from Sayyidna Abayd bin Hamal. Sadaqah from the side will be counted but its example is like flowing water"," whoever reaches for it will get it. Narrator named Farrukh has stated that the place is still the same today"," the person who reaches there gets it"," then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave Sayyiduna Abayd bin Hamal at the place of \""Jarf\"" which means \""Jarf\""."""
"4521","Sayyidna Abaid bin Hamal (RA) narrates that I said to the Messenger of Allah (PBUH): I asked him for a place called \Malh\"" and he gave it to me. Do you know which place you gave him? You gave him running water"," so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took that place back from him."""
"4522","Sayyidna Safwan bin Ya'ila narrates this statement of his father: I participated in the Battle of Tabuk with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. I consider this to be my greatest good deed. I had a laborer with me. He had a fight with a man. She has forgotten. When the other person pulled his hand, the front teeth of the chewing person broke. This case was presented in the presence of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he declared these teeth useless and he said: \Would this person had let his hand remain in your mouth so that you would have chewed his hand.\"" (The narrator says: I think this is an example in the tradition) You chew like a cow."""
"4523","Sufyan bin Abdullah narrates the statement of his two aunts, Sayyidna Ya'ila and Sayyidna Salama, that we participated in the Battle of Tabuk with the Prophet, may God's prayers and peace be upon him. There was a man living in Makkah with us. He used to come to the service of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to ask him to give him his diet. Then the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A person goes to his brother and bites him like a bull and then he comes to demand about it. You will not get any right. The narrator says that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left him."
"4524","This same hadith is narrated along with another chain of transmission, it contains these words that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He will not have any marriage, so the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left him like that."
"4525","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates that the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The partner has the right to intercede and intercession is made in everything."
"4526","Sayyiduna Abu Rafi' (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The neighbor has more right to intercede in his immediate place."
"4527","Amro bin Sharid narrates that Sayyidna Sa'd (may Allah be pleased with him) made a deal with Sayyidna Abu Rafi' (may Allah be pleased with him), or perhaps Sayyidna Abu Rafi' (may God be pleased with him) made a deal with Sayyidna Sa'd (may God be pleased with him). Sayyidna Abu Rafi' said: I heard the Prophet (peace be upon him) saying: \The neighbor has more right to intercede in his neighborhood.\"" If I had not heard this"," I would not have given you this place."""
"4528","Amro bin Sharid narrates: I and Sayyidna Abu Rafi’ (RA) came to Sayyidna Sa’d. Sayyidna Abu Rafi’ (RA) said: “You should buy my share in my house.” Sayyidna Sa’d said: “I don’t want to buy it.” Then someone suggested that you buy it from him. Allahu Anhu said: I will give it to him in exchange for five thousand dirhams, and I will have to pay it immediately, then Sayyiduna Saad said to him: I cannot pay you more. Sayyiduna Abu Rafi' said: If I had not heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: \The neighbor has more right to buy the land in his neighborhood\"""," then I would not have left five thousand dirhams and sold it for four dirhams."""
"4529","Sharid bin Suwayd narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The partner has more right to intercede, even if he obtains it or leaves it."
"4530","Amro bin Sharid narrates the statement of his father that he sold another part of his house. Another partner was with him, so this partner said to him: I have more right to buy it than anyone else."
"4531","Amro bin Sharid narrates the statement of his father that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The neighbor has more right to his \Saqb\"". Asked them what is meant by \""Saqb\""? So they replied: The neighborhood (in the place)."""
"4532","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has ruled that anything that is jointly owned by two people can be interceded in and cannot be divided, whether it is land or a garden, it is not permissible for a man to sell it unless he obtains the permission of his partner. In one hadith it is said that if a person sells such a place and does not inform his partner, then the partner will be more entitled to the place. In this hadith, the words \distributed\"" have been narrated only by the narrator named Abdullah bin Idris"," and he is Sahib Thaqa and Hafiz."""
"4533","Amro bin Sharid narrates that Sayyidna Sa'd, may God bless him and grant him peace, made a deal with Sayyidna Abu Rafi', may Allah be pleased with him, in the house of Sayyidna Abu Rafi', may Allah be pleased with him. Sayyidna Sa'd, may Allah be pleased with him, said to him: I will not pay you more than four dirhams. Karta) \Saqab\"" means to be close to a place."""
"4534","Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever creates something new in our religion that has nothing to do with it, that thing will be rejected."
"4535","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: Whoever does something about his wealth that is not permitted in the Book of Allah, that deed will be rejected."
"4536","Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever does something that is not according to our command, then that work will be rejected."
"4537","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa Radiyallahu Anha narrates that the person who does such a good deed \about which we do not have a command\"" will be rejected."""
"4538","Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Any work that does not have our command will be rejected.\"""""
"4539","Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa, may Allah be pleased with her, narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): No harm will be done to anyone."
"4540","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: A neighbor has the right to put a beam on his neighbor's wall, even if the other neighbor dislikes it, and the way for people to pass is seven cubits."
"4541","Sayyiduna Abu Saeed Radiyallahu Anhu narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: No one will be harmed if one does not harm oneself."
"4542","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: No harm will be done to anyone, and no one should forbid his neighbor from throwing his beam on his wall."
"4543","Qasim bin Muhammad states that when a guilty person makes a claim against a good person, about whom people think that person is lying, even if there is no issue between them, then the oath will not be taken from that good person."
"4544","Haritha bin Zafar narrates that a house was jointly owned by two brothers. They both erected a fence in the middle. Then they both died. Both of them left behind children. The children of each of them claimed that the fence of the land belonged to us and not to the other. Allah sent him to judge them. He calculated the wall as to whose land it meets and gave a decision in favor of the concerned person. They came back and told the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about this. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You have given a right decision."
"4545","Nimran al-Haritha narrates that his father narrated that some people came to the service of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a house that was common between the young men. So the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Sayyiduna Huzaifah (RA) to decide between them. Sayyiduna Huzaifah (RA) decided in favor of the one whose ropes were tied. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You have given the right decision. The narrator suspects that perhaps these are the words (that you have given a good decision)."
"4546","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: If a person becomes bankrupt and the person who sells his goods is found with him, then that person who sells will be more entitled to that thing than other creditors."
"4547","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said: “Whoever sells an item, and the person who bought it becomes bankrupt, and that person finds his item with him,” then he (the seller) will be more entitled to that item."
"4548","Sayyidna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: A person who is declared bankrupt and has property belonging to another person and has not received any value for that property, then he will collect the debt along with other debts."
"4549","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this saying of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): If a seller of goods finds his goods with a person who has been declared bankrupt, and the first person has not received anything from the second person, the goods will be found by the seller. But if this other person has paid some of the price of the goods, then the amount that was left, the seller will be treated like other creditors in this respect."
"4550","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): After that, it is according to the previous hadith."
"4551","The sons of Sayyidna Ka'b bin Malik (RA) narrate their father's statement that the Prophet (PBUH) had prevented Sayyidna Mu'adh (RA) from disposing of his wealth 'due to the payment of a debt which was obligatory on the young man' and had sold this property."
"4552","Hisham bin Urwa narrates this statement that Abdullah bin Jafar came to Sayyiduna Zubair and said: I have bought such and such things for so much. Said: Ja'far's son has bought such and such thing for so much. When I tried to prevent him from disposing of it, Sayyidna Zubair (RA) said: I am also a sharer with him in this deal. So Sayyidna Uthman (RA) said: How can I prevent someone from disposing of a deal in which Sayyidna Zubair (RA) is a partner? The narrator of this tradition, Yaqoob, i.e. Qazi Abu Yusuf, says: I am of the opinion that in such a case the person concerned can be restrained from disposing of it. But if a thing has been bought or sold by a person before it is disposed of, then if it is in a valid condition, I will declare it valid. will Qazi Abu Yusuf says: Imam Abu Hanifa did not prevent us from possession, nor has he issued a fatwa about the prohibition of possession."
"4553","Makhool narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: He who is right has a hand and a tongue."
"4554","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: If a person dies and he has to pay a debt and he has to recover a debt from someone, it is his responsibility to pay it immediately and the debt he has to take will be collected at the appointed time."
"4555","Sayyiduna Jabir (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (PBUH) has established the right of \intercession\"" for something that has not been divided"," that has been divided and the limits have been determined"," and if the paths have separated"," then there will be no intercession in it."""
"4556","Sayyiduna Huzaifah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) maintained the testimony of the midwife (present at the time of the child's birth)."
"4557","Sayyiduna Hudhayfah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) maintained the testimony of the midwife (present at the time of the child's birth)."
"4558","Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says: The testimony of the midwife regarding the birth of the child will be accepted."
"4559","Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) says that the Prophet (peace be upon him) accepted the testimony of one man and two women in marriage."
"4560","It is narrated about Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) that he made it obligatory to pay twelve dirhams (on the husband)."
"4561","Sayyidna Imran bin Hussain Radiyallahu Anhu narrates that a man freed six slaves at the time of his death. This man had no property except these slaves."
"4562","Sayyidna Imran bin Hussain (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that a person belonging to the Ansar died. He left behind six slaves in Turka. (i.e. freed duku and allowed four to remain slaves)."
"4563","Sayyiduna Abu Umamah Dhi Allah Anhu narrates that a man freed six slaves, he had no wealth except these slaves, when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was informed about this, he became very angry about it, then he divided them and gave them one-third (i.e. freed two slaves)."
"4564","Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that Hind bint Utbah, who was the wife of Abu Sufyan, came to the service of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and she said: O Messenger of Allah! Abu Sufyan is a miserly man 'they don't give me enough money for me or my children' so I have to take it out on their ignorance 'will I be guilty of this? So the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You should acquire as much as is sufficient for you and your children."
"4565","Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: This is the “sanctuary” of Allah, the Most High, which Allah made honorable on the day He created the heavens and the earth, and He has placed these two mountains here. The thorn shall not be broken, the prey here shall not be driven away, the grass here shall not be cut, the fallen thing here shall not be picked up, but may be picked up to declare. Sayyidna Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: O Messenger of Allah! The people living in Makkah cannot live without using Azkhar, goldsmiths also use it and it is also used in homes. The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The order of Azkhar is different (i.e. it is permissible to cut it)."
"4566","Sayyidna Zaid bin Khalid Jahni (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) was asked about gold or silver that had fallen, and the Prophet (PBUH) said: Remember the mark of the thread tied on the mouth of this (bag) and announce it for a year. If it comes, you will pay it. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the lost camel. Let it remain there. Its stomach and its feet are with it. It will reach its own water and eat leaves. Until its owner feeds it. The Prophet (peace be upon him) was asked about the (lost) goat."
"4567","Amro bin Shuaib narrated his grandfather's story regarding his father that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the lost camel and he said: Its belly and its feet are with it. He will go to the wolf, so you catch him."
"4568","Sayyidna Hibban bin Abu Jubla narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every person has more right to his wealth than his parents, his children and all other people."
"4569","Sayyidna Zaid bin Khalid (RA) narrates that a person came to the Prophet (PBUH) and asked: What do you say about the lost camel? So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) became angry, his face turned red, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is your connection with him? His feet and his stomach are with him, he will reach water by himself and eat leaves from trees until his owner comes to him. He said: Then what do you say about the lost goat? So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You catch her, because either you will find her, or one of your brothers will find her, or the wolf will find her."
"4570","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amro bin Al-Aas (RA) narrates that a person belonging to the Muzaina tribe came to the service of the Prophet (PBUH) and said: O Messenger of Allah! If someone breaks the rope, what do you say about it? So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In this and similar (other things), the hand will not be cut off for stealing an animal. Will there be an order? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: For stealing something like this, whipping will be done. For stealing a fruit from a tree, hands will not be cut off. Therefore, if the fruit stolen from there is equal to the value of the shield, then the hand will be cut off, but if it is not worth that much, then the hand will not be cut off. Or get something dropped? So what will be the ruling about it? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You should keep announcing it throughout the year. If its owner comes, pay it. Otherwise, use it. Whenever its owner comes to you, you shall pay it. If something is found in an uninhabited town or at the end of the road, it is the order to pay one-fifth of the treasure that comes out of it. The person asked: If a lost goat is found, what is your order about it? He said: You will find it, or one of your brothers will find it, or a wolf will find it. Therefore, he was asked about it as his brother's lost thing. The man said: What is your opinion about the lost camel? The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: He does not care. Its belly and its feet are with it. It will eat itself and drink water until its owner reaches it."
"4571","Sayyiduna Ali bin Abu Talib (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said: A will cannot be made for a murderer."
"4572","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): A murderer does not inherit."
"4573","Amro bin Shuaib narrates this statement from his grandfather regarding his father: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A murderer does not get anything from his inheritance."
"4574","Sayyiduna Umar bin Al-Khattab (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) has said that the murderer gets something (that is, he does not get anything from the inheritance). A similar tradition has been narrated by other people."
"4575","A similar tradition is transmitted by other people."
"4576","Zayd bin Aslam narrates this statement of his father: Sayyidna Umar bin Al-Khattab (RA) appointed his slave to be the overseer of the pasture. Be gentle with the Muslims, avoid the curse of the oppressed, because it is answered, you are a little sheep, let the owner of the goats enter the pasture, but do not let the animals of Uthman bin Affan and Abd al-Rahman bin Auf enter. They will come and say: O Commander of the Faithful! (Help us!) Shall I give them up? Providing water and mercury to these people is easier for me than providing dinars and dirhams, by Allah! These people think that we have violated them even though this is their territory, about which they used to fight with each other in the age of ignorance. And while living in the same area, they have accepted Islam, by this caste! In whose power is my life! If I did not want to provide wealth to the Mujahideen in the way of Allah, then I would not have prevented people from entering a place the size of a pillow (i.e. I would not have declared it a public pasture)."
"4577","Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates this statement of Sayyidna Saab bin Jathama (RA): The Prophet (PBUH) said: Pasture belongs only to Allah and His Messenger."
"4578","Amro bin Shuaib narrates the statement of his grandfather about his father that Sayyiduna Bilal, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to the service of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he had the tithe of his land with him. Sufyan bin Wahhib wrote a letter to Sayyiduna Umar and asked him about it, and Sayyiduna Umar said: He will pay you what he used to pay the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), i.e. one-twentieth of the produce of this place."
"4579","Amro bin Shuaib narrates his grandfather's statement regarding his father that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Pasture is only for Allah and His Messenger."
"4580","Sayyidah Umm Salama (RA) narrates that once she was sitting with the Prophet (PBUH) two men came to serve him, and there was a dispute between them regarding inheritance, which was about some things that had become old. If he finds something, he will get a piece of hell, which he will bring around his neck on the Day of Judgment. The narrator says that both of them started crying. One of them said: The right that I was demanding is actually the right of my companion. The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: No! Both of you go and examine it and take its portion, then each of you shall make it lawful for your partner."
"4581","This tradition is narrated along with another chain of transmission, but it contains these words: He said: Whoever among you I give judgment on the basis of evidence according to my opinion, and he will get a fair share as oppression."
"4582","Sayyidah Umm Salma (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that I was sitting with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and there was a veil between me and the people."
"4583","Sayyida Zainab bint Abu Salama (RA) narrates that Sayyid Umm Salama told her about the Prophet (PBUH) that he heard the sound of some people arguing at the door of his room. If I give a verdict in favor of a Muslim, then it will be a piece of Hell."
"4584","Sayyidah Zainab bint Umm Salama (RA) narrates this tradition on the authority of her mother that the Prophet (PBUH) said: You people come to me with a case, one of you may be faster than the other in presenting his argument. Do it because I would have cut a piece of hell for him. One hadith has these words: Now it is his will to obtain it or to give it up."
"4585","Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) once came to me and he was very happy. He said: O Ayesha! Do you know that Majzamd Laji came to me, he saw Usamah and Zayd (they were both sleeping) with a cloak covering their parts, but their feet were visible, so he said: These two are father and son."
"4586","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me once. He said: Do you know that Majzamd Laji looked at Osama bin Zayd who was lying with his father, and he said: These two are father and son."
"4587","Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that once a physicologist came, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was also there, Sayyida Usama bin Zayd and Zayd bin Haritha were both lying down. The person said: These are the feet of the father and son. Narrated Ibrahim bin Saadnami: Sayyidna Zayd Radiyallahu Anhu was the owner of red and white color while Sayyidna Osama was like night (black)."
"4588","Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that once the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to her, he was very happy and his face was shining with happiness. He said: Have you heard? What Majizzumdulji said about Zayd and Osama: He saw only their feet and said: These feet belong to the father and the son."
"4589","Sayyidna Abdullah Bin Zubayr narrates that Zam'ah had a slave girl with whom he used to have intercourse. This slave girl says that another person had intercourse with her. Meanwhile, Zam'ah died and she became pregnant. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: As far as the inheritance is concerned, he will get it, but as far as your affairs are concerned, you should hide from him because he is not your brother."
"4590","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that Sa'd and Abd bin Zam'ah sat next to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and began to argue. My brother Utbah gave me this will. He said: When you go to Makkah, you should see the son of the slave girl of Zamaa and take him in your arms because he is my son. Abd bin Zamaa said: O Messenger of Allah! He is the son of my father's maidservant and my brother, who was born on my father's bed. When the Prophet saw the clear resemblance of this child with Atba, he said: O Abd bin Zamaa! You will get it because the child belongs to the one who sleeps. You cover this boy."
"4591","Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that Sa'd bin Abi Waqqas and Abd bin Zam'ah brought a case about the son of the maidservant of Zam'ah. Sa'd said: O Messenger of Allah! This is the son of my brother Utbah bin Abi Waqqas. My brother made a promise to me about him that this is his son. You should liken him to Qutiba. Abd bin Zamaa said: This is my brother who was born on my father's floor by his maidservant. The narrator says; The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) likened it to Qutbiyah, which is clearly similar to Qutbiyah. He said that you will get a child because a child gets a bedridden person and an adulterer gets deprivation. The narrator says: After that, the child never saw Sayyida Saudah."
"4592","This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"4593","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may God be pleased with her) narrates that Qutiba bin Abi Waqqas made a promise to her brother Zayd bin Abi Waqqas that the daughter of the concubine Zam’ah is from me. And said: This is my brother. This is the son of my father's maidservant, who was born in my father's bed. These two came to the service of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. This is my nephew, about whom my brother made a promise to me. Abd bin Zam'ah said: This is my brother, the son of my father's maidservant, who was born on my father's bed. You will get it. Then the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The child will be considered as an infidel and the adulterer will be deprived. The reason for this was that the Prophet (PBUH) had seen its similarity with Utba. Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: This boy never saw Sayyida Soudah (may Allah be pleased with him) until he died."
"4594","Abu Bakr narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Wahb narrated to us: my uncle narrated to us: Yunus narrated to us. And Abu Bakr narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Uzzayz narrated to us: Salamah narrated to us: from Aqil. And Abu Bakr narrated to us: Abu al-Azhar narrated to us: Yaqub narrated to us: my father narrated to us: from Salih, and Ibn Ishaq. And Abu Bakr narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Ma'mar informed us. And Abu Bakr narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Hani and Abd al-Karim ibn al-Haytham said: Abu al-Yaman narrated to us: Shu'ayb narrated to us. And Abu Bakr narrated to us: Yusuf ibn Sa'id narrated to us: Hajjaj narrated to us: [Layth?] narrated to us. And Abu Bakr narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik al-Daqiqiyy narrated to us: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us: Sufyan ibn Husayn informed us. All of them narrated from Ibn Shihab. And Layth said: Ibn Shihab narrated to us: from Urwah: from Aisha: from the Prophet ﷺ, to the same effect."
"4595","A narrator named Muhammad narrates that there was a disagreement between Sayyidna Umar bin Khattab and Sayyidna Mu'azbin Afraa about something. These two men appointed Sayyidna Abi bin Ka'b as an arbiter. Sayyidna Umar narrated the whole incident to them. This payment is obligatory on you. So Sayyiduna Umar took an oath and said: Because of my oath, I am absolved from him. Take this thing, it is yours."
"4596","Hasan bin Thumamah narrates that once Sayyidna Huzaifah (RA) recognized his camel which had been stolen. He went to the Muslim judge with a case about it. According to the court decision, Sayyidna Huzaifah (RA) had to take an oath. So he announced the compensation of his oath: I give you ten dirhams. He refused. He said: I give you twenty dirhams. He refused. He said: I give you thirty dirhams. He refused. He said: I will give you forty dirhams. When he refused, Sayyiduna Huzaifa said: Leave my camel. Then he swore that it was his camel, which he had neither sold nor given to anyone."
"4597","Muhammad Bin Jubayr narrates his father's statement that he had paid ten thousand dirhams in exchange for his oath, and then he said: By the Lord of this mosque! And by the Lord of this grave! If I had been truthful in swearing in my oath, but this is something that I have given ransom in exchange for my oath."
"4598","It is narrated that Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) ordered forty dirhams for a hunting dog, one goat for a goat guard dog, and ordered a large pot of grain for a field guard dog, while he ordered a large clay pot for a house guard dog. Therefore, it is necessary that while receiving this compensation, he should reduce it."
"4599","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: Whoever builds a building on the land of another person and builds it with his permission, then he will be required to pay the price, and whoever builds a building there without the owner's permission, then this building will be demolished."
"4600","Amro bin Shuaib narrates his grandfather's statement regarding his father: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rejected the testimony of a cheating man, a cheating woman, a person who has a grudge against his brother, and a house servant."
"4601","Amro bin Shuaib narrates his grandfather's statement regarding his father that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The testimony of a man who betrays, a woman who betrays, a man who is severely punished, a woman who is severely punished, who has a grudge against his brother will not be accepted."
"4602","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The testimony of a man who betrays, a woman who betrays, a man who is severely punished, a person who has a grudge against his brother, and a servant of the house against his family is not valid."
"4603","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said while giving a sermon: Remember that the testimony of a cheating man, a cheating woman, a person who has a grudge against his brother, and a person who has been violated is not valid."
"4604","Amro bin Shuaib narrates his grandfather's statement regarding his father that the Prophet, may God's prayers and peace be upon him, said: The unfaithful man, the unfaithful woman, the person on whom the limit has been issued, and the person who bears testimony against his brother while bearing a grudge against him, their testimony is not valid."
"4605","Shaabi states that Qazi Shareeh used to accept the testimony of a person belonging to a religion against a person belonging to the same religion. He did not accept the testimony of a Jew against a Christian or a Christian against a Jew, but the problem of Muslims was different because he accepted the testimony of any Muslim against all other religions."
"4606","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am leaving two things between you, you will not go astray after they are (joined): the Book of Allah and my Sunnah, these two will not be separated until they reach me at the reservoir."
"4607","Sayyidna Ka’b bin Asim Ash’ari (RA) narrates that I heard the Prophet (PBUH) saying: “Allah has given me refuge in three things regarding my Ummah: They will not remain hungry, they will not agree on misguidance, and they will not perish."
"4608","Sayyidna Abaid bin Hamal (RA) narrates that I said: O Messenger of Allah! What do I pick from the yellow tree? So the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: That which the camel's feet could not reach."
"4609","Marwan Jafar says that my father told me that once in Kufa, there was a dispute between Sayyidna Mughira bin Shuba and Musqila bin Habira. I have more right to say that he is closer than me. Musqala said to them: The reason for this is that I left Sayyidna Ali bin Abu Talib (RA) among the emigrants and the Ansar and the great people of Iraq and joined Sayyidna Muawiya (RA) and used to wield the sword with him, and he appointed me as governor, so I freed Banusamah bin Lui for him. And they were rejoicing with their wives and playing with their children. Your tongue was long. You were miserly. Oh Masqala! These are the things you are talking about today. As far as you are concerned about leaving Sayyiduna Ali, you have done it. You have not done this out of love for the people of Syria, but you have done it because of your hatred for the people of Iraq. As far as you saying that you have freed Banusama bin Lui, a trusted companion of Sayyiduna Ali, trusting in you, has freed him. By Allah! You did not associate yourselves with them, nor did you free them from your wealth. As for my staying in Taif, the reason for this is that Allah has afflicted me with the trial of the family, which He has not afflicted you with."
"4610","Narrated by Sayyidna Abdullah bin Amro bin Al-Aas, may Allah be pleased with him: The Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The wine of Umm al-Khabayth is (the root of all evils).” Whoever drinks it, Allah will not accept his prayers for 40 days."
"4611","Sayyidna Zayd bin Khalid (RA) narrates, 'I heard the Prophet (PBUH) say this during his sermon in Tabuk: \Wine is a combination of sins.\"""""
"4612","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (RA) narrates: I heard the Prophet (PBUH) saying: \Alcohol is the root of evil and the greatest sin. Whoever drinks it"," he can attack the honor of his mother"," his grandmother"," his aunt.\"""""
"4613","Narrated by Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (RA): The Prophet (PBUH) said: \Wine is the root of all evils.\"""""
"4614","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: I heard Sayyiduna Umar Radiyallahu Anhu saying this on the pulpit of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: \When the order of sanctity of wine was revealed"," it was made from five things: grapes"," wheat"," barley"," dates and honey.\"""""
"4615","Sa'ib bin Yazid narrates: Once Sayyiduna Umar (RA) came to the people. He said: \I smelled alcohol from such and such a person.\"" I asked him what it was. So he said: He has taken talapia. I am inquiring about alcohol. If he becomes intoxicated"," I will flog him. Then Sayyiduna Umar r.a."""
"4616","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates (this saying of the Holy Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as a valid hadith: \Every intoxicant is forbidden"," and every intoxicant is khamr. Whoever drinks alcohol in this world and dies while drinking it regularly"," he will not drink it in the Hereafter.\"""""
"4617","This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"4618","This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"4619","This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"4620","Narrated by Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA): The Prophet (PBUH) said: \All intoxicating things should be forbidden and all intoxicating things are forbidden.\"""""
"4621","Narrated by Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA): The Prophet (PBUH) said: \All intoxicants should be forbidden and all intoxicants are forbidden.\"""""
"4622","Narrated by Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA): The Prophet (PBUH) said: \All things that are intoxicating should be curdled and anything that is intoxicating is forbidden.\"""""
"4623","Narrated by Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him: The Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said: \Every intoxicating thing is forbidden"," and every intoxicating thing should be bowed down.\"""""
"4624","Narrated by Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA): The Prophet (PBUH) said: \Every intoxicating substance is Haraam and every wine is Haraam.\"""""
"4625","Narrated by Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA): The Prophet (PBUH) said: \All intoxicants should be bowed down and all intoxicants are prohibited.\"""""
"4626","Narrated by Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA): The Prophet (PBUH) said: \All intoxicating things should be forbidden and all intoxicating things are forbidden.\"""""
"4627","Narrated by Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA): The Prophet (PBUH) said: \Let every intoxicating thing be bent and intoxicating is forbidden.\"""""
"4628","Narrated by Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA): The Prophet (PBUH) said: \Every intoxicating thing is Haram and every intoxicating thing is forbidden.\"""""
"4629","Narrated by Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him: The Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Let every one of you be humble.\"""""
"4630","Narrated by Sayyiduna Ali bin Abu Talib, may Allah be pleased with him: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Every intoxicating thing is forbidden"," and whatever intoxicates in large quantities"," even a small amount of it is forbidden.\"" The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \""I do not declare intoxicants as halal.\"""""
"4631","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa, may Allah be pleased with her, narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, \every intoxicating thing is forbidden"," and a small amount of anything that intoxicates is forbidden"," and even a sip of any drink that intoxicates is forbidden.\"""""
"4632","Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): “Anything that intoxicates is forbidden.”"
"4633","Sayyiduna Abdullah Bin Masoud Radiyallahu Anhu says: This is the sip that will intoxicate you."
"4634","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud Radiyallahu Anhu says: \Any intoxicant is forbidden.\"" This means a drink that intoxicates you."""
"4635","This hadith was mentioned before Sufyan bin Abdul Malik on the authority of Sayyidna Ibn Mas'ud, may Allah be pleased with him. Sayyidna Abdullah bin Mas'ud, may Allah be pleased with him, said: This is the sip that will intoxicate you. Abdullah bin Mubarak said: This is a false tradition."
"4636","The tradition that is narrated with reference to Hamad, \Intoxicating food is forbidden"," it means the cup that causes intoxication\"" is correct"," it is the opinion of Ibrahim Nakhai."""
"4637","Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about \Ba'ta\"" (a certain type of alcohol)"," and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \""Any drink that intoxicates is forbidden.\"""""
"4638","Sayyida Aisha Sidiqah (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) was asked about \Ba'ta\"" (a certain type of alcohol)"," and the Prophet (PBUH) said: \""Any drink that intoxicates is forbidden.\"""""
"4639","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about “bata” (the narrator says: Taba means the sleep of honey), then the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: “Any drink that intoxicates is forbidden.”"
"4640","Aamir bin Saad quotes the saying of the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, regarding his father: \I forbid you even a small amount of anything that intoxicates you in excess.\"""""
"4641","Aamir bin Saad quotes the saying of the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, regarding his father: \I forbid you even a small amount of anything that intoxicates you in excess.\"""""
"4642","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I prepared sleep in a daba (a special vessel for making wine) in order to present it as a gift to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on that day when he was fasting, when it was time to break the fast, I picked it up and brought it to his service. He inquired: O Abu Huraira! what is it I said: O Messenger of Allah! My parents are a sacrifice to you. This is Nabeez, which I have prepared for you. I knew that you would fast today, so I want you to use it. The Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: Bring it near me. When the Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, examined it, he was excited. He said: Hit it against this wall, because he who does not believe in Allah and the Last Day will drink it."
"4643","Sayyidna Nu'man bin Bashir (RA) narrates: I heard the Prophet (PBUH) saying: \Khumrangur"," date"," raisin"," wheat"," barley and corn are prepared and I forbid you from anything that is intoxicating.\"""""
"4644","Narrated Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar: I heard Sayyiduna Umar, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying from the pulpit of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: \And then! O people! When the prohibition of alcohol was revealed"," it was made from five things: grapes"," honey"," dates"," wheat"," and barley; everything that covers the intellect (i.e. produces intoxication) was curdled. O people! I wished for three things that the Holy Prophet"," peace and blessings of God be upon him"," would explain to us about them: Dada (part of k and ast)"," kalala and usury (some forms of usury).\"""""
"4645","Narrated Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar: I heard Sayyiduna Umar, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying from the pulpit of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: \Afterwards! O people! When the prohibition of alcohol was revealed"," it was made from five things: grapes"," wheat"," barley"," dates and honey.\"""""
"4646","Imam Shaabi narrates: I heard Sayyidna Numan bin Basheer Radiyallahu Anhu describing this minbar (the narrator says:) i.e. from the pulpit of Kufa, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Indeed"," wine is made from dates"," kushmush"," wheat"," barley"," and honey.\"""""
"4647","Sayyidna Nu'man bin Basheer Radi Allahu Anhu cites this as a \marfu'\"" hadith that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Wine is made from five things: wheat"," dates"," raisins and honey"," and everything that veils the intellect is called 'Khamr'."""
"4648","Sayyidna Numan bin Basheer (RA) narrates the saying of the Prophet (PBUH): Dates make wine, Raisins make wine, Wheat makes wine, and honey makes wine."
"4649","The same hadith has been narrated along with another chain of narrators on the authority of Sayyidna Numan bin Basheer (RA), however, there has been an illusion in quoting the narrator."
"4650","Sayyidna Nu'man bin Bashir (RA) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (PBUH): Remember that wine is made from grapes, raisins, dates, wheat and barley."
"4651","Sayyidna Nu'man bin Bashir (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said: Wheat makes wine, which makes wine, raisins make wine, dates make wine, and honey makes wine, and I forbid you anything intoxicating."
"4652","Abdullah bin Abu Hazil narrates that Sayyiduna Abdullah took an oath and stated that when the prohibition of alcohol was revealed, under the order of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the pots for making alcohol were broken and the dates and raisins (which were used for alcohol) were discarded."
"4653","Amro bin Shoaib narrates his grandfather's statement regarding his father that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Anything that produces intoxication in large quantities is prohibited even in small quantities.\"""""
"4654","Sayyidna Khawat bin Jubayr Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): “Anything that causes intoxication in large quantities, even a small quantity of it is forbidden."
"4655","Amro bin Shuaib narrates the statement of his grandfather regarding his father that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every intoxicant is forbidden and anything that produces intoxication in large quantities is also forbidden in small quantities."
"4656","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: A portion (i.e. a cup) of something that causes intoxication, even a small amount (i.e. a small amount) of it is forbidden."
"4657","This tradition is narrated along with another chain of transmission, however, it contains these words: \Even a sip of it is forbidden.\"""""
"4658","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: \One cup of anything that causes intoxication is forbidden.\"""""
"4659","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A single sip of anything that causes intoxication is forbidden."
"4660","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Whatever causes intoxicants"," its awqiyyah is forbidden.\"""""
"4661","Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Even a single sip of anything that causes intoxication is forbidden."
"4662","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says: Even a single sip of anything that causes intoxication is forbidden. This hadith is \suspended\""."""
"4663","Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Even a single sip of anything that causes intoxication is forbidden.\"""""
"4664","Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Even a single sip of anything that causes intoxication is forbidden."
"4665","Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Even a single sip of anything that causes intoxication is forbidden."
"4666","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) says: Alcohol and intoxicating drinks have been forbidden. This tradition has been narrated along with some other isnads. \Intoxicants are prohibited.\"" While some narrators have quoted these words: \""Anything that produces intoxication in large quantities"," even a small quantity of it is forbidden.\"" Some narrators have also narrated the fatwa of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) regarding intoxicants (which is as follows)."""
"4667","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) says: Whatever causes intoxication in large quantities, even a small quantity of it is forbidden."
"4668","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) says: Whatever causes intoxication in large quantities, even a small quantity of it is forbidden."
"4669","One of the descendants of Sayyidna Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates the statement of a member of his family, that he asked Sayyida Ayesha, may Allah be pleased with her, about Nabeez. She said: O my son! Allah Ta'ala has not declared the khamrakwas haram because of its name, but has made it haram because of its consequences."
"4670","Amro bin Shuaib narrates his grandfather's statement regarding his father: Some people came to the service of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: O Messenger of God! We do Zatiyar and drink it in the morning and evening. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Drink it, but (remember) every intoxicant is forbidden. He said: O Messenger of Allah! We break (the rush of intoxication) through water. The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Whatever causes intoxication in large quantities"," even a small amount of it is forbidden.\"""""
"4671","Amro bin Shoaib, regarding his father, narrates the statement of his grandfather that some people came to the service of the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him. He said: O Messenger of God! We make nabi zatiar and drink it with food. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Drink it, but avoid anything intoxicating. He repeated what he said, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has forbidden you to consume even a small amount of that which causes intoxication in large quantities."
"4672","Abd al-Rahman bin Abu Laila narrates: My father and I came to the service of Sayyiduna Ali bin Abu Talib, may God be pleased with him. He fed us dinner, then he gave us a drink."
"4673","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that when I mentioned a few pots in front of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), a villager said: There is nothing wrong with the pots."
"4674","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates about the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he (may God bless him and grant him peace) said to the delegation of the tribe of Abdul Qais: You people, do not drink from muqeer, muqeer, daba hantam, and Mazada (all these are different vessels for preparing alcohol)."
"4675","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): When a person goes to his Muslim brother and feeds him, then a person should eat and not ask him for anything."
"4676","Sayyiduna Abu Burda (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: You people should drink (ordinary drink) in a \muzfat\"" (special vessel) but not drink intoxicating drink. In one hadith there are these words: Thou shalt not drink intoxicating drink."""
"4677","Ibn Burida narrates this statement of the Holy Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, regarding his father: I forbade you from certain vessels, so drink from whatever vessels you want, but do not drink intoxicants."
"4678","Ibn Buridah quotes the saying of the Holy Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, regarding his father, that we had previously forbidden you to drink in certain vessels, 'You drink in whatever vessel you want', but do not drink anything intoxicating."
"4679","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that once we camped with the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in Wadi Batha (after that the narrator has narrated the entire hadith, which has these words:). \I forbade you to visit the graves. Now visit them because they will remind you of the hereafter. I forbade you to use the meat of the sacrifice for more than three days"," so now you should eat it and store it."""
"4680","Zaid bin Aslam narrates that I used to recite Nabi zatiaar for Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) in the morning, which he used to drink in the evening, and in the evening, the Nabi used to recite zatiaar, which he used to drink in the morning, but he did not allow him to get excited."
"4681","Sayyidna Umar bin Al-Khattab (RA) says, \I am a fast drinker who digests the meat of camels in our stomachs.\"""""
"4682","Saeed Bin Musayyib narrates that the Nabi was sent to Sayyiduna Umar (R.A) on the occasion when he was supposed to come, but he came late."
"4683","Saeed bin Musayyib narrates that the people of Thaqeef tribe humiliated the Prophet and came to Sayyiduna Umar (RA), then Sayyiduna Umar (RA) found that she had become hot, so he called for water and mixed it thirty times."
"4684","Umar bin Maimon narrates that I performed Hajj twice with Sayyiduna Umar, I heard him say: We pray to the Prophet so that the meat in our stomachs does not torment us (i.e. it is properly digested)."
"4685","A narrator named Saeed narrates that once a villager drank the Prophet from the vessel of Sayyiduna Umar (RA)."
"4686","Uthman ibn Abul-Aas narrates that Sayyiduna Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, passed by the vessel of a man of the Thaqif tribe, and he said: \This nabeez"," let me have it. It was brought to his service.\"" Sayyiduna Umar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," took it and said that it was sharp."""
"4687","Utbah bin Farq says that once I came to Sayyiduna Umar's service with a plate of sweetmeats. I placed them in front of him. All Muslims are blessed with this thing. I said: No! This thing is only available to rich people. Sayyiduna Umar said: You take it, I don't need it. The narrator narrates: Meanwhile, they asked for food in my presence, so fat meat and hard bread were brought to them. Then he let him stay for a little while. Then he gave me water and drank it himself. Then he said: O Utba! We cook camel meat every day and feed its good sirin meat to guests or common Muslims and eat the neck meat that does not rot, which you have seen just now, after that the Prophet eats it so that the meat is digested in our stomach."
"4688","Abdullah bin Mubarak narrates that Abdullah bin Umar Umari asked Imam Abu Hanifa (RA) about the drink, and he told us that people have narrated this hadith to us regarding your father, that he said: If you are worried about it, then increase its strength through water."
"4689","It is narrated about Sayyidna Umar bin Al-Khattab (RA) that he had given a complete whipping to a person whose mouth had been sprinkled with alcohol."
"4690","Sha'bi states that a person drank Nabeez from the vessel of Sayyidna Ali (Radi Allahu Anhu) - this is about the place of Safin - He became intoxicated, then Sayyidna Ali (Radi Allahu Anhu) reprimanded him."
"4691","Amir narrates that a villager drank Nabeez from an old musket and became intoxicated, so Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) stopped him. This is a messenger and these two narrations are not proven."
"4692","Sayyidna Maald bin Abu Wada' Sahmi (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that once on a hot summer day, the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) circumambulated the House of Allah. He asked some people of Quraysh for water to drink. So one of them sent from his house, a maid came, she had a vessel, in which there was a Nabi Dhimm made of raisins. Even if it was covered by a piece of wood, when he brought the vessel near you, you felt a sharp smell from it. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned it. The person said: O Messenger of Allah! If it is forbidden, then don't drink it. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called for this vessel again and did the same thing with it. The person said the same again. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called for a bucket of Zamzam and put it in the vessel and said: \When your drink becomes strong"," do this with it.\"""""
"4693","Sayyidna Matal bin Abu Wada'a narrates that once the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said after circumambulating the House of Allah: Give me something to drink! So the Prophet of Raisin was humiliated in your service. You gave him something to drink and then returned him. I said: O Prophet of Allah! Is it forbidden? By Allah! It is a drink, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) remained silent. They asked him this question again, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) remained silent again. He said: O Messenger of Allah! Is it forbidden? By Allah! This is the special drink of the people of Makkah. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Bring it back to me! Then he ordered the people to add water to it, so the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began to drink it sip by sip."
"4694","Malik bin Thaqafi narrates that I asked Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) about the smell of Teznabeez, and he said: Once the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was sitting in a gathering. It was brought to the service of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took his blessed face to it and smelled it. Then he brought the face back and returned it. When the person had left Batha, the person came back and asked: Is it haram or halal? So the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) put his head close to it and felt its bitterness and added water to it, then drank it. This hadith has been narrated in the same way, however, it has been authentically narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him): \Anything that causes intoxication in large quantities"," even a small quantity of it is forbidden.\"" This tradition has been passed before."""
"4695","Sayyidna Abu Mas'ud Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that once the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) felt thirsty near the Kaaba. The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mixed that water in it and drank it. A person said: O Messenger of Allah! Is it forbidden? The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No!"
"4696","Sayyidna Abu Mas'ud Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that once the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) felt thirsty, he was circumambulating the Kaaba at that time, so Prophet Zakam Shakiza was brought to his service. The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not accept him. Is it forbidden? The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: No! You come to me with a bucket of zam-zam. Then the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mixed that water with it and drank it, and then he started circumambulating."
"4697","Sayyidna Abu Mas'ud Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that I remember about the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that a vessel was brought to the service of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in which the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was present. Is it forbidden? The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took hold of this vessel, then he called for a bucket of zam-zam and mixed that water in it, then he drank this drink, then he said: When your Prophet becomes zatiz, end his fastness with water."
"4698","Sayyiduna Abu Mas'ud Ansari (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) was asked about Nabeez: Is it halal or haram? So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is lawful."
"4699","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the following about the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): A person was brought (to him) who had become intoxicated due to drinking Nabeez of dates, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) flogged him."
"4700","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates: A person was brought to the service of the Prophet (PBUH) who had become intoxicated due to drinking Nabeez, so the Prophet (PBUH) flogged him."
"4701","Sulaiman Taymi says: There is no harm in drinking Nabeez."
"4702","Sayyidna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that Sayyidna Abu Talha (may Allah be pleased with him) came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I have bought some wine for the orphans under my care. The Prophet (PBUH) repeated this three times."
"4703","Alqamah bin Wail narrates the statement of his father: A man named Suwayd bin Tariq asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about alcohol, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade him from drinking this wine. The man said: I prepare it for medicine."
"4704","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about wine: Should it be made into vinegar? So he said: No!"
"4705","Sayyidna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that there was an orphan boy under the care of Sayyidna Abu Talha (may Allah be pleased with him) Sayyidna Abu Talha (may Allah be pleased with him) bought wine for him. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No!"
"4706","Sayyidna Anas bin Malik (RA) narrates that Sayyidna Abu Talha (RA) told me this: He had some property of the orphans, and he used it to buy alcohol. Then the order of sanctity of alcohol was revealed. I have bought wine through him. This is before the revelation of the order of wine. So the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) instructed me to break the vessel and pour out the wine. I attended your service three times."
"4707","Sayyidah Umm Salma (RA) narrates: We had a goat that was sick. The Prophet (PBUH) inquired: What happened to your goat? We told him that it was epilepsy. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Why do you not benefit from its skin? We said: He is dead. The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Its tanning makes it halal, just as a head made of wine is halal."
"4708","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that one day we were participating in a battle, 'We felt hungry,' until we distributed another two dates.' Then we reached the seashore. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) inquired: Do you have any part of it? Nafi' narrated that when those people came to the service of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and told him about it, the Prophet (peace be upon him) inquired: Do you have any share of it? People answered: Yes! The people asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Do you have any part of it? People answered: Yes! People offered it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he ate it."
"4709","It has been narrated about Abd al-Rahman bin Abu Huraira that he asked Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him): Shall I skin the fish that floats on the water (after death)? Abdullah ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: \The fish that swims in the water is dead.\"""""
"4710","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Sarjis (RA) who is an old man, narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said: Allah has slaughtered the fish in the sea for the children of Adam."
"4711","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every animal in the sea has been declared pure by Allah for the children of Adam."
"4712","Amro bin Dinar says that I have come to know (that is, the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said:) Allah has slaughtered everything in the sea for the children of Adam."
"4713","Sayyidna Jabar bin Abdullah (RA) narrates this saying of the Holy Prophet (PBUH): “Eat the animal that the sea appears and throws out, but do not eat the one that you find dead (the narrator doubts these words here) that floats on the water."
"4714","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): “When the animal swims on the water, do not eat it, and when the water recedes, then eat it, and what is found on the shore, eat it too.” The narrators have differed in quoting the authenticity of this tradition."
"4715","Sayyidna Jabir (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: Eat what the sea takes out or what it brings up, and do not eat what dies in the sea and floats in the water."
"4716","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that eat the fish that the sea throws out or that appears, and do not eat the fish that you find floating on the water."
"4717","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) says: Eat what the sea throws out or abandons it and retreats or hunts it, and do not eat what dies in it and then floats on the water."
"4718","This tradition is transmitted as a \suspended\"" tradition along with another document."""
"4719","Sayyiduna Abu Bakr Sadiq (may Allah be pleased with him) says: Allah has slaughtered everything in the sea for you."
"4720","Sayyiduna Shareeh (may God be pleased with him) who was a companion of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has slaughtered everything in the sea for the children of Adam."
"4721","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) says: I testify about Sayyidna Abu Bakr (RA) that he said: A fish floating on water (i.e. a dead fish) is lawful for a person who wants to eat it."
"4722","It has been narrated with the same authority that he said: (After death) the fish that floats on the water is halal."
"4723","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that I heard Sayyidna Abu Bakr Sadiq (RA) saying: Allah has slaughtered everything in the sea for you, so eat them all because they have been slaughtered."
"4724","Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) says: I testify about Sayyidna Abu Bakr Sadiq (RA) that he ate fish that floated on the water."
"4725","Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) says that Sayyidna Abu Bakr Sadiq (RA) said: All kinds of fish are slaughtered."
"4726","Sayyidna Umar bin Al-Khattab (RA) says: Every kind of fish is slaughtered and every kind of grasshopper is slaughtered."
"4727","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that Allah Ta'ala has said: \For you the game of the sea and its food has been made lawful for you. It is Zadrah for you and for those who travel.\"" Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah Radiyallahu Anhu says: What is meant by his food is what he throws out."""
"4728","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) says about this decree of Allah Ta'ala: \The hunting of the sea and its food have been made lawful for you.\"" Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) says: Hunting means something that is hunted"," and eating means something that is thrown out into the sea."""
"4729","It is narrated about Sayyiduna Abu Ayyub that he was going on a sea voyage with some of the companions of the Holy Prophet, peace be upon him. They found a dead fish floating on the water. When people asked him about it, he asked: Is it clean? There has been no change in it (i.e. the flowers have not started coming)? People answered: Yes! (Pure is) So Sayyiduna Abu Ayyub Radiyallahu Anhu said: Eat it and take my share from it (i.e. keep it). The reason for this was that he was fasting at that time."
"4730","Jablah bin Atiya narrates that some of the companions of Sayyiduna Abu Talha (radiyallahu anhu) found a fish floating on the water (after his death)."
"4731","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: Slaughtering the mother of a child in the womb of an animal is considered as slaughtering it, whether its hair has come out or not. A narrator named Ubaidullah has stated this: But if he comes out of the mother's womb, then he will be ordered to be slaughtered until blood comes out of his womb."
"4732","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two kinds of blood have been made lawful for us and two kinds of dead bodies have been made lawful. Dead (things) are fish and locusts."
"4733","Sayyiduna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) was asked about the baby in the belly of an animal, which comes out dead, and the Prophet (PBUH) said: \Eat it if you wish.\"""""
"4734","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Eat the baby that comes out of the womb of the mother (female animal). Narrator Abu Sudnami has narrated that eat the baby in the camel's stomach."
"4735","Sayyiduna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) narrates this about the Prophet (PBUH): He (PBUH) was asked about a she-camel that has a baby in its belly, and the Prophet (PBUH) said: When you slaughter it, mention the name of Allah, then slaughtering the mother of the baby in that womb will be counted as slaughtering the baby."
"4736","Sayyidna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) narrates that we asked the Prophet (PBUH) 'We said: If a person slaughters a camel or a cow or a goat and finds a child in its belly, should he eat it or throw it away? So the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you want, eat as much as you like, because slaughtering his mother will be counted as slaughtering him."
"4737","Sayyidna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (SAW): Slaughtering the mother of a child in the womb of an animal is considered as slaughtering it."
"4738","Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the following as a \marfu'\"" hadith: Slaughtering the mother of a child in the womb is considered as slaughtering her."""
"4739","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): As for the child in the womb of an animal, slaughtering its mother is considered slaughtering."
"4740","Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Slaughtering the mother of a child in the womb (of an animal) is considered as slaughtering it. Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: Slaughtering the mother of a child in the womb (of an animal) is considered as slaughtering it."
"4741","Abu Salamah and Sulaiman bin Yasarbayan say that they have come to know the saying of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that whoever wants to delay can offer sacrifice until the end of the month."
"4742","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) says: Whoever has the capacity and still does not offer sacrifice, then he should not come to our mosque. Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) sacrificed two horned bulls, one of which he slaughtered on behalf of himself and his family, and the other he slaughtered on behalf of those members of his Ummah who could not."
"4743","Saeed bin Al-Masayyib narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (RA) that he used to say: \Whoever has ease (financial ability) but does not offer sacrifice"," then he should not enter our mosque.\"""""
"4744","On the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyib on the authority of Sayyidina Abu Hurairah (may God be pleased with him) who said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, sacrificed two goats, both of which had crooked horns and acorns on the back."
"4745","Sayyidah Umm Salama (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the first ten days of Dhul-Julj begin and a person wants to make a sacrifice, he should not cut his hair and nails."
"4746","Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: The order of sacrifice has abolished every sacrifice that preceded it."
"4747","Abolished every previous ablution, the fasting of Ramadan has abrogated every fast, the ablution of Janabat has abrogated every ablution, and Zakat has abrogated every charity."
"4748","Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Zakat has canceled every charity in the Qur’an, Ramadan fasting has canceled every fast, Ghusl Janabat has canceled every bath, and Eid sacrifice has canceled every sacrifice."
"4749","Sayyiduna Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-Aas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that a person came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: I have been commanded that the day of Eid al-Adha is the Eid that Allah has appointed for this Ummah. Can I slaughter an animal if I have given it? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No! However, if you trim your nails, trim your moustache, clean your pubic hair, then your sacrifice will be complete in the presence of Allah."
"4750","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said: \I have been ordered to sacrifice"," but it is not obligatory.\"""""
"4751","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: \Sacrifice has been made obligatory on me"," but it has not been made obligatory on you people. I have been ordered to offer the Eid-ul-Adha prayer"," but you have not been ordered to do it.\"" This tradition is narrated along with another document."""
"4752","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: \Whatever you spend silver (i.e. money) on"," the most excellent thing in it is to sacrifice on the day of Eid al-Adha.\"""""
"4753","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade eating the meat of a camel that eats filth and drinking its milk. \Only goods can be loaded on it.\"" People will not slaughter it until it has eaten fodder for forty days."""
"4754","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet sent Badil bin Warqa Al-Khuza’i (may Allah be pleased with him) on a camel to announce in the paths of semen that the throat and lips will be slaughtered and do not hasten to take life and the days of semen are days of eating and drinking and spending time with wives."
"4755","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa narrates that I said: O Messenger of Allah! Can I sacrifice by taking a loan? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Yes! It is a debt that will be repaid."
"4756","Nafi bin Jubayr narrates the statement of his father that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The days of Tashriq are the days of slaughter for all (i.e. sacrifices can be made during these days)."
"4757","This tradition is also narrated along with another document."
"4758","Sayyidna Jabir bin Mut'im narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: All the days of Tashreeq are the days of slaughter (i.e. they can be sacrificed)."
"4759","Sayyiduna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) sacrificed a horned ram and then prayed: \O Allah! This is on behalf of me and on behalf of every member of my Ummah who could not sacrifice.\"""""
"4760","Sayyidna Jabar bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that I was with the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the Eid-ul-Adha prayer. When the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished the prayer and finished the sermon, he came down from his pulpit. Harass is towards the person who cannot perform the sacrifice."
"4761","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this about the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): He slaughtered two black sheep, one of them was from his Ummah and the other was from him and his family."
"4762","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: Whoever has the capacity and still does not offer sacrifice, should not come to our Eidgah."
"4763","Asim bin Kalib narrates this statement of a person belonging to the Ansar: We attended a funeral with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. We came to the grave. Q: So-and-so lady has invited you and your companions. The Prophet (PBUH) went to this lady. When all the people were seated and the food was brought, the Prophet (PBUH) extended his blessed hand towards her. The people also extended their hands and the Prophet (PBUH) started eating. Meanwhile, he stopped his hand. The narrator says: We were sitting in the place where children sit with their fathers. saw that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had vomited what he had eaten, so all those people hit their children's hands and dropped the herbs in their hands. I sent someone to Baqi' to look for my goat, but he could not find that goat. I found out that my neighbor had also bought a goat. So I sent a message to him, but he refused. We could not get it. Then this goat was sent by the man's wife, so the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: Feed it to the prisoners."
"4764","Asim bin Kalib narrates the statement of a man from the tribe of Muzaina regarding his father: A woman belonging to the Quraysh prepared food for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and invited him and his companions. It is said that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had started eating, when the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took a morsel, then he put it away from her and said: I have felt the taste of this goat's meat as if it had been slaughtered without the permission of its owner. The woman said: O Messenger of Allah! It belongs to my brother and my brother loves me the most. If there was a better goat, it would not have been difficult for us to slaughter it."
"4765","Asim bin Kalib narrates with reference to his father that an Ansari narrated this hadith to me: When I was a young child, I went with my father to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). After that, he mentioned the previous hadith, which reads as follows: This woman said: I sent a message to my brother Amir bin Abu Waqqas because a goat was bought from Baqi', but my brother was not there, so his wife took this goat. sent me"
"4766","Abdul Wahid bin Ziyad states that I inquired from Imam Abu Hanifa: Where did you get the issue that a person disposes of another's wealth without his permission, then he will give the profit as charity? So Imam Abu Hanifah said: I obtained it from the hadith narrated by Asim bin Kalib."
"4767","Sayyidna Muqadam bin Maad Yakarb (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) declared certain things haram on the day of the Battle of Khyber. will make it forbidden (the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said:). \Whatever the Messenger of Allah has forbidden is like that which Allah has forbidden.\"""""
"4768","Sayyidna Muqadam bin Maadikarb (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have been given the Book and that which is similar to it (i.e. the Sunnah has been given). We will declare it haram. (The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, Yarawi said:). It is not like 'eating any sharp-toothed beast or eating a donkey' it is not permissible to pick up the fallen thing of a contracted person' but if it is something that is not needed, then the ruling will be different."
"4769","Sayyidna Khalid bin Waleed (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade eating the meat of horses, mules, donkeys, sharp-toothed beasts (maybe these words are the words:) on the day of the Battle of Khyber."
"4770","Sayyiduna Khalid bin Waleed, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade eating the meat of horses, mules, donkeys, and sharp-toothed beasts on the day of the Battle of Khyber."
"4771","This tradition is narrated along with another chain of transmission, but this tradition is weak because Waqidi has stated that Sayyidna Khalid bin Waleed (RA) accepted Islam after the conquest of Khyber."
"4772","Yahya bin Muqadam narrates that he heard his grandfather narrating: Once I and ten people of my tribe, perhaps a little more than that, had not eaten for twenty-two days. They had blinded the horse to be slaughtered. So they would do evil, because the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) declared the property of Dhimmis, the meat of donkeys, horses and mules to be haram. Then Sayyidna Qald (RA) ordered these people to give them two grains of grain and one aid and said that when we encounter any campaign, we will inform them."
"4773","Sayyidna Khalid bin Waleed (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) forbade domesticated donkeys, horses and mules. The narrator says: His chain of transmission is not authentic because Sayyiduna Khalid (may Allah be pleased with him) accepted Islam after the Battle of Khyber."
"4774","Majzat bin Zahir narrates the statement of his father: who had pledged allegiance to the Holy Prophet under the tree, he narrates that once he was afflicted with an illness, the Holy Prophet sent him a message to use donkey milk and broth (as medicine), but he did not like this food (yadwa)."
"4775","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that we used to eat the meat of horses. The narrator says that we inquired: And of mules? He replied: Not that."
"4776","Sayyiduna Jabir (RA) narrates that those people used to eat horse meat during the time of the Prophet (PBUH). The narrator states: A narrator named Ata has narrated that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the meat of mules and donkeys."
"4777","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that once we were traveling with the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and we ate horse meat and drank (mare's) milk."
"4778","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that on the day of the Battle of Khyber, we ate the meat of horses, mules and donkeys, then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us to eat the meat of mules and donkeys, but he did not forbid us to eat the meat of horses."
"4779","Sayyiduna Jajar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to feed us the meat of horses, but he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us the meat of donkeys."
"4780","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that on the day of the Battle of Khyber, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us to eat the meat of domestic donkeys, but he allowed us to eat the meat of horses."
"4781","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered us to eat the meat of horses, but the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us to eat the meat of donkeys."
"4782","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) forbade eating the meat of pet donkeys."
"4783","Sayyida Asmaa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that during the time of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) we slaughtered a horse and ate its meat."
"4784","Sayyida Asma bint Abu Bakr (RA) narrates that we had a horse during the time of the Holy Prophet (SAW) and it started to die, so we slaughtered it and ate its meat."
"4785","Sayyida Asmaa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that during the time of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) we kept a horse and we (slaughtered) it and ate its meat."
"4786","Sayyida Asmaa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that during the time of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) we slaughtered a horse."
"4787","Sayyidna Jabar bin Abdullah (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) forbade eating cat meat and using its value."
"4788","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that a rabbit was served in the service of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I was asleep at that time, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) held its back for me. When I woke up, the Prophet (peace be upon him) gave it to me to eat."
"4789","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about a mouse that grunts in ghee or fat, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If it is ghee, then throw away the ghee around it, and if it is in the form of an obstacle, then use it for another purpose, but do not eat it."
"4790","Sayyidna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) was asked about a rat that grunts in ghee and olive oil, and the Prophet (PBUH) said: Use it for something else. Do not eat it. This tradition is transmitted as a \suspended\"" tradition along with another chain of transmission."""
"4791","Sayyidna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) says that if there is thunder in olive oil in the chuhaghi, then you should profit from it, but do not eat it."
"4792","Sayyidna Abu Waqid Laithi (RA) narrates that when the Prophet (PBUH) came to Madinah, people used to cut the humps of camels and the meat of the tusks and eat them."
"4793","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said: The part of a live animal that is cut off will be considered dead."
"4794","Imam Muhammad bin Hasan Shaibani narrates the following statement of Abd al-Rahman bin Laila regarding Imam Abu Hanifa: I went to a farmer with Sayyidna Hudhaifa, may Allah be pleased with him, and he brought food to us, and we ate it. Then Sayyiduna Huzaifa (RA) said: We came to him last year too, and he brought me a drink in the same vessel. I told him that the Prophet (PBUH) forbade us to eat or drink in gold or silver vessels, or to wear silk clothes (the Prophet (PBUH) said:). \These two things are for the polytheists in this world"," but they will be for us in the Hereafter.\"""""
"4795","This tradition is also narrated along with another chain of transmission, however, it contains these words: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying these words: \Do not drink from gold and silver vessels and do not eat from them.\"""""
"4796","It is narrated about Sayyiduna Huzaifa that once he asked for water to drink and a farmer brought water to him in a silver vessel. Sayyidna Huzaifa caught it and threw it away and then said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allaah be upon him) forbade us to drink or eat from gold or silver vessels, and he also prohibited us from wearing silk and jewelry and from sitting on them. What is forbidden?"
"4797","Amro bin Shuaib narrates the statement of his grandfather regarding his father that a person attended the service of the Holy Prophet, his name was Abu Thaalba, he said: O Messenger of Allah! I have some trained dogs 'you tell me about hunting through them! So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If your dogs are trained, then eat the prey they catch for you, regardless of whether they get a chance to slaughter it or not. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Even if he himself eats some of it (yet you can eat it), this person said: O Messenger of Allah! You tell me about my bow! The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Eat whatever your bow (i.e. arrow) shoots. He asked: Whether it was slaughtered or not. The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If he hides from you, then until he is lost, until you find no other mark in him than your arrow (then you can eat him). This person said: O Messenger of Allah! You tell me about the potions of the Magi when we use them under compulsion? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You can wash them and then eat in them."
"4798","Shaabi narrates that Sayyidna Udi bin Hatim asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: I shoot my arrow, but I reach the target after one day. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: When you capture the prey and there is no mark or scratch on it other than your arrow, then you should eat it. (Here the narrator is in doubt about a word) This is because you do not know whether you have hunted it or someone else has hunted it. Likewise, when you release your dog and it catches the prey and you reach the prey, then you should slaughter it. Killed and even ate some of it, then you should not eat the prey (the narrator has doubts about a word here). The reason is that this animal has kept that prey for itself. Eat! Because you don't know whether your dog has killed him or another dog has killed him."
"4799","Sayyidina Adi bin Hatim (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) was asked about hunting, and the Prophet (PBUH) said: When you start to shoot your arrow, take the name of Allah over it. If you find the prey in such a state that it is dead, then eat it."
"4800","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: (The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)) forbade the slaughter of a Magian, the prey of his dog or the prey of his bird."
"4801","Sayyidna Abu Tha'laba Hashani (RA) narrates that I said: O Messenger of Allah! We live together with the idolaters. We do not have separate pots and pans. The narrator says that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If possible, try to avoid them. But if there is no space, wash it with water. Water will purify it, then cook (food) in it."
"4802","Sayyiduna Abu Thalaba Khoshni (RA) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (PBUH) that when you throw your fish and it is absent from you for three days, then you reach it, then eat it, while it does not smell bad."
"4803","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that a person asked the Prophet (PBUH): O Messenger of Allah! What is your ruling about a person who forgets to recite the name of Bismillah while slaughtering? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The name of Allah is present on the tongue of every Muslim. My narrator has disagreed about one word here."
"4804","Ibrahim says about a Muslim who forgets to recite Bismillah while slaughtering. Ibrahim says: There is nothing wrong with that."
"4805","With another chain of transmission, it is narrated about Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may God be pleased with him) that he did not think there was anything wrong with it."
"4806","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) says: When a Muslim slaughters an animal and does not mention the name of Allah on it, he can eat it because the word Muslim also contains a name of Allah."
"4807","Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says: There is no harm in eating the bread cooked by a Magi."
"4808","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) says: His name alone is sufficient for a Muslim. If he forgets to recite Bismillah, he should eat it after reciting Tabsmillah and mentioning the name of Allah."
"4809","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (RA) narrates that some people said: O Messenger of Allah! Some people slaughter meat and bring it to us. We do not know at that time whether they mentioned the name of Allah while slaughtering it or not. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \You eat it while mentioning the name of Allah.\"""""
"4810","Al-Khajri ibn Salat narrates the statement of his uncle that he attended the service of the Prophet (peace be upon him), then he was returning from the service of the Prophet (peace be upon him) and he passed by some people. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) inquired: Did you recite this Surah (Fatihah)? He said: Yes! The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then accept it, by my life! Whoever eats something with false breath (it will be wrong), you have eaten it with true breath."
"4811","Al-Khajri bin Salat narrates the statement of his uncle that he attended the service of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and then according to the previous hadith, in which there are these words: You should eat it with the name of Allah, because whoever eats it with false breath, he is doing wrong."
"4812","This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"4813","Al-Khajri ibn Salat narrates the statement of his uncle that he went to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and then according to the previous hadith, however, it has these words that he said: You people will pay us for it. So I said: I will ask the Prophet (peace be upon him) about this first."
"4814","Dahhak bin Muzahim narrates: I Hasan bin Abul Hasan, Makhool, Amro bin Dinar and Taus gathered in \Masjid Khaif\"" these people began to argue loudly"," these people began to argue about tazeez"," on this Taus said: who was the favorite person of all: you should be quiet! I am narrating to you the hadith that I heard on the authority of Sayyiduna Abu Darda"," may Allah be pleased with him: The Prophet"," may God bless him and grant him peace"," said this: Allah has made certain things obligatory upon you"," so do not waste them"," and He has set certain limits for you"," do not transgress them. Do not oblige him"," because it is a mercy from your Lord"," accept it! (After that"," Taus said:) We say what our Lord and our Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has said: All things are in the hands of Allah Almighty. He orders everything. He will also reward everything. At this all the people stood up and these people liked (i.e. adopted) the saying of the Taos."""
"4815","The hadiths that have been narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) are mentioned here (this is an addition to the original book). 4729 Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) had a race between horses and the one who reached the limit first was declared successful."
"4816","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (pbuh) used to train horses and compete between them."
"4817","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) ran from \Hafiyyah\"" to \""Taniya Al-Wadaa\"" among trained horses and ran from \""Tanayyah Al-Wadaa\"" to Masjid Banuzriq among untrained horses."""
"4818","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet used to train horses."
"4819","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made a race between trained horses from Thaniya al-Wada to Masjid Banuzreeq. My horse took me and climbed the wall. A narrator named Sufyan has stated that there is a distance of five or six miles from Saniya Al-Wada to Hafiyyah, while the distance from Saniya Al-Wada to Masjid Banuzariq is up to one mile. A narrator named Abu Mas'ud has narrated these words in his tradition: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) conducted a competition between untrained horses from Saniyyah al-Wada to Masjid Banuzreeq. Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I was also among those who participated in this race."
"4820","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) conducted a competition between horses. Sayyiduna Abdullah Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: I was also among those riders, I went ahead of the people and my horse took me to Masjid Banuzreeq."
"4821","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) had a race between horses. Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that I went ahead and was close enough that my horse would have taken me and climbed the wall of the mosque, which was very small."
"4822","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet made a competition between trained horses from Hafiyyah to Saniyyah al-Wada, while he made a competition between untrained horses from Saniyyah al-Wada to Masjid Banuzreeq. The narrator narrates: Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) was also among those who won this competition."
"4823","Sayyidna Jabar bin Abdullah (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) had a competition between horses. I was also riding one of them."
"4824","Abul Baid al-Mazah bin Zubayd Bayan says that I made a competition between the horses of the pilgrims. Hakim bin Ayyub was the governor of Basra in those days. When we reached the race field and the horses came there, we thought that if we went to Sayyidna Anas bin Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, and asked him about it, did those people also run in the same way during the time of the Prophet, peace be upon him, then it would be appropriate. Ibn Malik (R.A.) appeared in his service. He was in his palace. We said: O Sayyidna Anas! Did you people used to fight horses during the time of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? So he replied: Yes! The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had entered his horse in the competition, whose name was \Sanjah\"""," and it came first."""
"4825","The same hadith has been narrated by Ibn Mubashir along with another chain of transmission from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Anas (RA), which is similar to the tradition narrated by Yazid."
"4826","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that whenever the camel of the Prophet (PBUH) Qaswa joined the race, it used to go ahead. Saeed bin Musaib narrates that once a person came and his camel overtook the Qaswa. The people were very sorry that a camel overtook the camel of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"4827","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that no one could win a race with the camel of the Prophet (PBUH) in a race, it always went ahead."
"4828","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that no one could get ahead of Qaswa. Once a villager brought a young camel. He fought with Qaswa and he got ahead of him. This caused a lot of trouble for the Muslims. He said: O Messenger of Allah! A person has gone beyond the Quswa', so he said: In this world, whomever Allah gives high, He sometimes lowers him."
"4829","Saeed bin Musayyib narrates that Qaswa was the camel of the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him. “Whatever race she participated in, she would lead the way. Words are:) when wanting to see someone high."
"4830","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that a villager fought with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"4831","Sayyidna Imran bin Hussain (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) has said this: There is no reality of Jalab, Janab and Shaghar in Islam, and the person who practices any of them has nothing to do with us."
"4832","Basramzni quotes his grandfather's statement regarding his father saying that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no truth in Jalab and Janab. Narrator Ibn Abawais stated that Jalab means that a man pulls a horse from behind in order to overtake him, and Janab means that he creates an obstacle in front of another horse so that it does not win."
"4833","Abu Ubaidnami, the narrator, has quoted these words in the hadith of the Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him: There is no truth in Jalab and Janab. The narrator says: Jalab occurs only in two things, one is in horse racing, and this is the way that a man rides on the back of a horse and pulls the horse. It is forbidden to buy its fruits and receive its charity. Rather, it is ordered that he should go to people and collect charity from them. Run and win, because that horse will be less tired than a horse with a rider on it."
"4834","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (PBUH) that there is no reality of ``Atira'' and ``Fa'ar'' in Islam, and there is no reality of ``Jilb'' and ``Janb'' either. The narrator says: Atirah is the animal that was slaughtered by the people of the dangerous tribe in the age of ignorance."
"4835","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: Whoever enters his horse among other horses in such a way that he is not sure that it will get ahead of him, then there is no harm."
"4836","A narrator named Hasan has narrated this tradition about Sayyidna Ali (RA) that the Holy Prophet (PBUH) said to Sayyidna Ali (RA): I am appointing you as a horse-runner. I am entrusting you with the responsibility of those who join the race, which the Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, has entrusted to me. So when you reach Maitan (Abu Abd al-Rahman says: This means the place from where the race was to start), form a line of horses and announce three times: Someone is going to fix the bridle, someone is going to lift the boy, someone is going to put (the end of the bridle) on the horse's head (i.e. if it is not If no one gives you an answer, then say Allahu Akbar three times and leave him, then Allah will help him for the sake of whomever He wills from among His creatures. When Sayyiduna Ali (RA) would come to the last mark of the race, he would draw a line and make two men stand face to face on both sides of this line. Declaring and if you doubt about it, you would declare them both successful and when you declare the two equal, then make the last limit which is the smaller of the two."
"4837","Dahhak bin Muzahim narrates: I Hasan bin Abul Hasan, Makhool, Amro bin Dinar and Taus gathered in \Masjid Khaif\"" these people began to argue loudly"," these people began to argue about tazeez"," on this Taus said: who was the favorite person of all: you should be quiet! I am narrating to you the hadith that I heard on the authority of Sayyiduna Abu Darda"," may Allah be pleased with him: The Prophet"," may God bless him and grant him peace"," said this: Allah has made certain things obligatory upon you"," so do not waste them"," and He has set certain limits for you"," do not transgress them. Do not oblige him"," because it is a mercy from your Lord"," accept it! (After that"," Taus said:) We say what our Lord and our Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has said: All things are in the hands of Allah Almighty. He orders everything. He will also reward everything. At this all the people stood up and these people liked (i.e. adopted) the saying of the Taos."""
"4838","The hadiths that have been narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) are mentioned here (this is an addition to the original book). 4729 Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) had a race between horses and the one who reached the limit first was declared successful."
"4839","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (pbuh) used to train horses and compete between them."
"4840","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) ran from \Hafiyyah\"" to \""Taniya Al-Wadaa\"" among trained horses and ran from \""Tanayyah Al-Wadaa\"" to Masjid Banuzriq among untrained horses."""
"4841","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet used to train horses."
"4842","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made a race between trained horses from Thaniya al-Wada to Masjid Banuzreeq. My horse took me and climbed the wall. A narrator named Sufyan has stated that there is a distance of five or six miles from Saniya Al-Wada to Hafiyyah, while the distance from Saniya Al-Wada to Masjid Banuzariq is up to one mile. A narrator named Abu Mas'ud has narrated these words in his tradition: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) conducted a competition between untrained horses from Saniyyah al-Wada to Masjid Banuzreeq. Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I was also among those who participated in this race."
"4843","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) conducted a competition between horses. Sayyiduna Abdullah Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: I was also among those riders, I went ahead of the people and my horse took me to Masjid Banuzreeq."
"4844","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) had a race between horses. Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that I went ahead and was close enough that my horse would have taken me and climbed the wall of the mosque, which was very small."
"4845","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet made a competition between trained horses from Hafiyyah to Saniyyah al-Wada, while he made a competition between untrained horses from Saniyyah al-Wada to Masjid Banuzreeq. The narrator narrates: Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) was also among those who won this competition."
"4846","Sayyidna Jabar bin Abdullah (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) had a competition between horses. I was also riding one of them."
"4847","Abul Baid al-Mazah bin Zubayd Bayan says that I made a competition between the horses of the pilgrims. Hakim bin Ayyub was the governor of Basra in those days. When we reached the race field and the horses came there, we thought that if we went to Sayyidna Anas bin Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, and asked him about it, did those people also run in the same way during the time of the Prophet, peace be upon him, then it would be appropriate. Ibn Malik (R.A.) appeared in his service. He was in his palace. We said: O Sayyidna Anas! Did you people used to fight horses during the time of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? So he replied: Yes! The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had entered his horse in the competition, whose name was \Sanjah\"""," and it came first."""
"4848","The same hadith has been narrated by Ibn Mubashir along with another chain of transmission from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Anas (RA), which is similar to the tradition narrated by Yazid."
"4849","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that whenever the camel of the Prophet (PBUH) Qaswa joined the race, it used to go ahead. Saeed bin Musaib narrates that once a person came and his camel overtook the Qaswa. The people were very sorry that a camel overtook the camel of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"4850","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that no one could win a race with the camel of the Prophet (PBUH) in a race, it always went ahead."
"4851","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that no one could get ahead of Qaswa. Once a villager brought a young camel. He fought with Qaswa and he got ahead of him. This caused a lot of trouble for the Muslims. He said: O Messenger of Allah! A person has gone beyond the Quswa', so he said: In this world, whomever Allah gives high, He sometimes lowers him."
"4852","Saeed bin Musayyib narrates that Qaswa was the camel of the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him. “Whatever race she participated in, she would lead the way. Words are:) when wanting to see someone high."
"4853","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that a villager fought with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"4854","Sayyidna Imran bin Hussain (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) has said this: There is no reality of Jalab, Janab and Shaghar in Islam, and the person who practices any of them has nothing to do with us."
"4855","Basramzni quotes his grandfather's statement regarding his father saying that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no truth in Jalab and Janab. Narrator Ibn Abawais stated that Jalab means that a man pulls a horse from behind in order to overtake him, and Janab means that he creates an obstacle in front of another horse so that it does not win."
"4856","Abu Ubaidnami, the narrator, has quoted these words in the hadith of the Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him: There is no truth in Jalab and Janab. The narrator says: Jalab occurs only in two things, one is in horse racing, and this is the way that a man rides on the back of a horse and pulls the horse. It is forbidden to buy its fruits and receive its charity. Rather, it is ordered that he should go to people and collect charity from them. Run and win, because that horse will be less tired than a horse with a rider on it."
"4857","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (PBUH) that there is no reality of ``Atira'' and ``Fa'ar'' in Islam, and there is no reality of ``Jilb'' and ``Janb'' either. The narrator says: Atirah is the animal that was slaughtered by the people of the dangerous tribe in the age of ignorance."
"4858","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: Whoever enters his horse among other horses in such a way that he is not sure that it will get ahead of him, then there is no harm."
"4859","A narrator named Hasan has narrated this tradition about Sayyidna Ali (RA) that the Holy Prophet (PBUH) said to Sayyidna Ali (RA): I am appointing you as a horse-runner. I am entrusting you with the responsibility of those who join the race, which the Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, has entrusted to me. So when you reach Maitan (Abu Abd al-Rahman says: This means the place from where the race was to start), form a line of horses and announce three times: Someone is going to fix the bridle, someone is going to lift the boy, someone is going to put (the end of the bridle) on the horse's head (i.e. if it is not If no one gives you an answer, then say Allahu Akbar three times and leave him, then Allah will help him for the sake of whomever He wills from among His creatures. When Sayyiduna Ali (RA) would come to the last mark of the race, he would draw a line and make two men stand face to face on both sides of this line. Declaring and if you doubt about it, you would declare them both successful and when you declare the two equal, then make the last limit which is the smaller of the two."
